00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.040
<i>miraculously.</i>

3
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.280
<i>We are navigating
under the Arctic ice cap</i>

4
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.640
<i>by dead reckoning</i>

5
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.160
<i>and five days from home.</i>

6
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.080
<i>After 25.000 nautical miles</i>

7
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.600
<i>the Sevastopol has deliberately
approached every navy in the world</i>

8
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.560
<i>and remained completely undetected.</i>

9
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:24.040
<i>The Podkova's stealth capability
has exceeded all expectations.</i>

10
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.920
<i>We are at this moment
the state of the art of war.</i>

11
00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.360
<i>The most fearsome killing machine</i>

12
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.240
<i>ever devised by man.</i>

13
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.680
<i>And we are impossible to find.</i>

14
00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.120
Captain. we have a submerged contact.
designated Semyon-83

15
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.480
exhibiting tonals
of a US Virginia-class submarine.

16
00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.400
Bearing 130°. drawing forward.

17
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.960
Chief of the Watch.
man battle stations silently.

18
00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.176
- Rig for ultra quiet.
- Officer of the Deck. ship status?

19
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.560
Ship's depth. 50 meters.

20
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.800
Bottom. 72 meters.

21
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.800
Clearance to the ice canopy.
21 meters.

22
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.920
- Distance to deep water?
- Two kilometers.

23
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.520
Aleutian Precipice in six minutes.

24
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.480
Ranging maneuver.
Helm. left 15 degrees rudder.

25
00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.800
Steady course 100°.

26
00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.360
Come up easy on a standard bell.

27
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.960
- Captain has the conn.
- Helm. aye!

28
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.560
Coming to course 100°.

29
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.080
Steady on course 100°.

30
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.320
Weapons Officer. range?

31
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.240
Firing solution is tracking
at a distance of 15.000 meters.

32
00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.400
Sir. that doesn't make sense.
Tonals this loud and clear?

33
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.240
<i>He must be closer than that.</i>

34
00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.840
Captain. firing solution just did
a step change to 10.000 meters.

35
00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.360
Nothing moves that fast.

36
00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.600
All solutions are matching.
The range is true.

37
00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.880
Helm. right full rudder
to course 270°.

38
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.560
Course 270°. aye.

39
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.160
We'll just walk away
and head for deep water.

40
00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.240
Contact bearing 160°.

41
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.160
Bearing rate zero?

42
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.400
He's there. turning with us again.

43
00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.200
He can see us.

44
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.760
Impossible. We're invisible.

45
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.440
Weapons. run diagnostics on sonar
and fire control.

46
00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.520
<i>Something isn't right.</i>

47
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.320
Sir. he's flooding his torpedo tubes!

48
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.400
Torpedo room. conn.
Load all torpedo tubes.

49
00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.480
Aye. sir.

50
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.400
- Check clear!
- Forward clear!

51
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.800
Aft clear! Ram torpedo!

52
00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.880
Ramming!

53
00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.160
Torpedo tubes loaded.

54
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.320
He's opened outer doors!

55
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.720
Weapons. flood tubes one
through four and open outer doors.

56
00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.520
Enter firing solution into tube two.

57
00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.120
Aye. Captain. Making tube two
ready in all respects.

58
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.320
Captain. he's provoking us.

59
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.600
He wants an excuse
to blow us out of the water.

60
00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.000
Enemy torpedo in the water.
bearing 200°.

61
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.400
1.000 meters and accelerating.

62
00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.560
Helm. left full rudder.
all ahead flank cavitate.

63
00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.200
My rudder is left full.
Answering all ahead flank cavitate.

64
00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.400
- Launch countermeasures.
- Launching countermeasures.

65
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.680
- Fire tube two.
- Firing tube two.

66
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.440
Our torpedo is away. Running hot.

67
00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.960
Enemy torpedo still homing.
range 800 meters.

68
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.416
He's blown through
our countermeasures.

69
00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.600
- Helm. right full rudder.
- Right full. Aye. sir!

70
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:21.880
- 600 meters.
- Diving Officer

71
00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.000
stand by to emergency
blow all main ballast tanks.

72
00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.256
- 400 meters.
- Chief of the Watch

73
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.160
- stand by the collision alarm.
- 200 meters.

74
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.016
This is the captain.
All hands brace for impact.

75
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.760
Enemy torpedo impact in

76
00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.920
five... four...

77
00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.800
three... two...

78
00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.560
one.

79
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.800
Impact!

80
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.760
What just happened?

81
00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:51.880
It's... It's gone.

82
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.000
- It missed us?
- No.

83
00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.040
It vanished like it was never there.

84
00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.760
Sonar. where is the enemy vessel?

85
00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:00.880
Bearing 330°

86
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.600
4.000 meters off our starboard bow.

87
00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.200
Our torpedo is running true.

88
00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.480
Impact with enemy submarine in...

89
00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.920
three... two... one.

90
00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.320
Where was the impact?

91
00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.800
Captain. enemy submarine
has vanished.

92
00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.200
It's gone. sir.

93
00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.160
I don't understand.

94
00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.080
He was never there.

95
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.160
We've been chasing a phantom.

96
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.640
It was right there.

97
00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.040
The instruments don't lie.

98
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.800
They lied to us today.

99
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.920
- Weapons. shut down our torpedo.
- Aye. Captain.

100
00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.320
Shutting down torpedo.

101
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.480
Secure from battle stations.

102
00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.520
This is why we have sea trials.

103
00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.080
There's a bug in the system.

104
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.360
A ghost in the machine.

105
00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.120
It's time to go home.

106
00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.520
Captain! Our own torpedo
is not responding.

107
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.680
It's coming right at us!

108
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.040
Our torpedo's homing

109
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.800
- range 400 meters!
- Oh. my God.

110
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.600
Wire command. Shut down our weapon!

111
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.440
Our torpedo's still closing

112
00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.200
- range 200 meters!
- Emergency!

113
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.760
Blow all main ballast tanks!

114
00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.080
Sound the collision alar...

115
00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.520
Food delivery.

116
00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.080
Hello?

117
00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.360
Designator.

118
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.720
Easy.

119
00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.120
Easy.

120
00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.640
Designator.

121
00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.120
India-Zulu-254.

122
00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.920
Bravo-Echo-11.

123
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.000
No. not yet.

124
00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.360
You need to ask me
the security question first.

125
00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.360
Oh. yeah. Sorry.

126
00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.000
What is the oath?

127
00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.920
We live and die in the shadows

128
00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.160
for those we hold close

129
00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.320
and for those we never meet.

130
00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.440
You can put it on the table.

131
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.400
Hey.

132
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.480
Welcome to the IMF.

133
00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.880
You made the right choice.

134
00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.480
Sir.

135
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.600
<i>Good evening. Mr. Hunt.</i>

136
00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.600
<i>It's been a long time.</i>

137
00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.000
<i>Our lives are the sum of our choices</i>

138
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.600
<i>and we cannot escape the past.</i>

139
00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.880
<i>30 years ago.
you were offered the choice.</i>

140
00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.800
<i>Join the IMF
or spend your life in prison.</i>

141
00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.000
<i>Because of
your unique natural talents</i>

142
00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.000
<i>your government forgave you.</i>

143
00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.480
<i>But we will never forget.</i>

144
00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:20.240
<i>Just as you will
never forget the death</i>

145
00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.040
<i>that brought you to us
all those years ago.</i>

146
00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.880
<i>This is to remind you of your oath
and allegiance to us.</i>

147
00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.200
<i>The stakes of this mission
are higher than ever.</i>

148
00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.720
<i>Your habitual rogue behavior
will not be tolerated.</i>

149
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.080
<i>Should you choose to accept.
it is imperative that you listen.</i>

150
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.320
<i>Your government
is searching for a key.</i>

151
00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.800
<i>Its purpose.
its vital importance to us</i>

152
00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.680
<i>is none of your concern.</i>

153
00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:02.880
<i>What should concern you</i>

154
00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.880
<i>is the involvement of
your friend Ilsa Faust.</i>

155
00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.600
<i>She killed a courier in Istanbul.</i>

156
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.360
<i>And we believe he was carrying</i>

157
00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:14.000
<i>one half of the key
we're searching for.</i>

158
00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.240
<i>Why she has chosen to interfere
in this affair is a mystery</i>

159
00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.560
<i>as are her whereabouts.</i>

160
00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.840
<i>What is certain</i>

161
00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.760
<i>is that your government
has put a price on her head</i>

162
00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.200
<i>and these bounty hunters
are out to collect it.</i>

163
00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.760
<i>They never bring
a fugitive back alive.</i>

164
00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.360
<i>And rarely in one piece.</i>

165
00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.720
<i>We believe they're headed for
the Arabian Desert's Empty Quarter</i>

166
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.200
<i>in search of your friend.</i>

167
00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:45.200
<i>Find the bounty hunters.
and you may just find her.</i>

168
00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.920
<i>Your mission.
should you choose to accept it</i>

169
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.320
<i>is to acquire the key
and deliver it to us.</i>

170
00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:55.440
<i>What happens to Ilsa after that
is up to you.</i>

171
00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.400
<i>As always. if any members
of your team are caught or killed</i>

172
00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.640
<i>the secretary will disavow
any knowledge of your actions.</i>

173
00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.160
<i>This message will self-destruct
in five seconds.</i>

174
00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.200
<i>Good luck. Ethan.</i>

175
00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:43.920
Come.

176
00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:32.880
Ethan.

177
00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.320
So. what are we dealing with?

178
00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:13.920
This "entity" has
multiple personalities

179
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.160
at times behaving
like a computer virus

180
00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.320
then a tapeworm. then a botnet.

181
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.480
Distorting any
and all digital information

182
00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:21.880
with which it comes in contact.

183
00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:22.960
Once infected

184
00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.920
nothing recorded. stored
or transmitted digitally

185
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.120
can be trusted as fact.

186
00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.800
At the outset. it concentrated
primarily on news and social media

187
00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:34.040
which was of little concern to us
as it often suited our purposes.

188
00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.200
Until six months ago

189
00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.280
when the entity breached

190
00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.480
Saudi Arabia's
General Intelligence Directorate.

191
00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.680
And assimilated
their top secret active learning AI

192
00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.920
before vanishing into the cloud.

193
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.080
Subsequent attacks increased
ten-thousandfold overnight

194
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.720
spreading exponentially.

195
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.560
Indicating that
the Entity has since become...

196
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.320
sentient.

197
00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.120
You're telling me
this thing has a mind of its own?

198
00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.960
Over the last three weeks alone

199
00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.520
it has accessed
our satellite telecommunications

200
00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.000
the Federal Reserve. the stock market
and the national power grid.

201
00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.240
The FAA. NASA and the combined
branches of our military.

202
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.360
And we're not alone.

203
00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.800
It has penetrated
the World and European Central Banks.

204
00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.960
Gained entry to the major defense.
finance and infrastructure systems

205
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:19.160
of Russia. India. Israel.
Australasia. all of Europe.

206
00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:22.160
And what did it do
to all of these systems exactly?

207
00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.240
Nothing.

208
00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.640
- Nothing?
- It came

209
00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.360
and it went. leaving fingerprints
where they could easily be found

210
00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:32.160
and sending a very clear message.

211
00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.320
"I shall return."

212
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:38.800
Whatever its ultimate goal is.
we're powerless to stop it.

213
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.800
The full force of its energy is
now directed at a single objective.

214
00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.640
The world's intelligence networks.

215
00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.960
The very truth as we know it.

216
00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.640
The entire intelligence community
is racing to archive

217
00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:53.600
hard copies of
our fact-positive knowledge bases

218
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:57.440
before our most secure data centers
are breached and corrupted.

219
00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.240
Which is only a matter of time.

220
00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:01.000
The Entity will know precisely

221
00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.840
how to undermine our every strength
and exploit our every weakness.

222
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.600
How to turn our allies into enemies

223
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.600
and our enemies into aggressors.

224
00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.240
Why not air-gap
our intelligence servers?

225
00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.440
Cut them off
from the outside world entirely?

226
00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:16.880
We already have.

227
00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:20.040
But servers require humans
to maintain them.

228
00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:23.000
And humans are the weakest link
in any security chain

229
00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:27.080
especially when dealing with
a godless. stateless. amoral enemy.

230
00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:30.920
One that has been patiently
listening. reading. watching.

231
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.120
Harvesting our deepest
personal secrets for years.

232
00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:38.880
Able to beguile. blackmail. bribe
or be anyone it wants.

233
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.680
And to manipulate us at will
through our total dependence

234
00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.560
on a carefully constructed
digital reality.

235
00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.800
An enemy that is everywhere

236
00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.200
and nowhere

237
00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.200
and has no center.

238
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.360
All right.
so what you're telling me is

239
00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:03.920
the most awesome goddamn intelligence
and tactical apparatus on the planet

240
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.880
has no way of killing this thing.

241
00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.200
You don't want to kill it. sir.

242
00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.200
You want to control it.

243
00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.000
And how do we do that. Mr. Kittridge?

244
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:19.760
The CIA's assets in the Kremlin
informed us that the Russians

245
00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:23.040
have focused the majority
of their intelligence activity

246
00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.280
on acquiring two halves
of a cruciform key.

247
00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.480
And what does it unlock?

248
00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.800
Not exactly sure.

249
00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.880
But the Russians seem to
believe that it somehow has

250
00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.720
the power to deactivate
our mysterious Entity.

251
00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.080
Though. ideally

252
00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:41.280
they hope to control it. harness it.

253
00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:43.560
Do you believe that. Kittridge?

254
00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:47.880
What matters is that
the rest of the world believes it.

255
00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.000
Japan. India. Germany
and the Brits believe it.

256
00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.720
And yet no one.
not even our closest allies

257
00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.520
have willingly whispered
one word of it to us.

258
00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:00.080
Which would indicate
that there's a global race on

259
00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.480
to acquire
the two halves of this key.

260
00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:07.720
Every nation in it for themselves.
not to kill this thing. sir

261
00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.160
but to weaponize it.

262
00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:14.400
And. in so doing. establish
a new. incontestable form

263
00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.960
of global dominance.

264
00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.480
How do we find this key first?

265
00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:20.920
Well. we know that a buyer is passing
somewhere through the Middle East

266
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.440
sometime in the next 72 hours.

267
00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.880
We believe that he already has
one half of this key.

268
00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:27.960
You believe.

269
00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.321
At this point. we can't be certain
it's not a counterfeit.

270
00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.440
How would you verify that?

271
00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.600
The only thing that can authenticate
one genuine half of the key

272
00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.720
is the other genuine half
of the key...

273
00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.000
its true mate. if you will.

274
00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.560
We think it's some sort of fail-safe.

275
00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:41.720
How do we find its mate?

276
00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:45.040
Well. we believe
the other genuine half of the key

277
00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.480
was in the hands of this woman.

278
00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:48.480
Who is she?

279
00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.920
Ilsa Faust.

280
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.440
Former British Intelligence.

281
00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.120
- Where is she now?
- She's dead. sir.

282
00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:55.880
She was. excuse me

283
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.440
killed by mercenaries
looking to collect a bounty.

284
00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:00.560
And who put up the bounty?

285
00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:03.080
Given her body of work.
could have been anyone.

286
00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.160
So anyone could have
her half of the key?

287
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:07.680
Not just anyone.

288
00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.560
I sent a man to find her.

289
00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.560
The only man that she would have
entrusted with her half of the key.

290
00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.000
Does he have it. Kittridge?

291
00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:19.240
Well. at present. I don't know that.
sir. He's refused to come in.

292
00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:20.880
Refused?

293
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.200
Who the hell is this guy?

294
00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:24.400
That's classified.

295
00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:27.000
I'm the goddamn
Director of National Intelligence.

296
00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.840
What exactly is it
I'm not supposed to know about?

297
00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.400
- The IMF.
- Mr. Kittridge.

298
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.480
- The world bank.
- No

299
00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.896
that's
the International Monetary Fund.

300
00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:37.120
- Mr. Kittridge.
- No. I mean the other IMF. Ours.

301
00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.640
What does it stand for?

302
00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.400
Impossible Mission Force.

303
00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.400
You're not serious.

304
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.160
I'm afraid he is.

305
00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.800
And what do they do exactly?

306
00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:48.720
It's just as the name implies.

307
00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.040
Whatever the rest of us can't.

308
00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:51.120
And who is in charge?

309
00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:53.216
They're not ones to take orders
in the traditional sense.

310
00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:54.360
We more or less...

311
00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:58.320
leave word.

312
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.320
Leave word.

313
00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.960
- Mr. Kittridge. sir.
- The IMF operates

314
00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.120
outside the community and
answers directly to the president.

315
00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.600
So. let me get this straight.

316
00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:10.760
When there's a mission
none of you can handle

317
00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:15.360
you just leave word
for a nameless man

318
00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:19.120
and hope he gets the job done.
Is that it?

319
00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:22.200
Should he choose to accept it.

320
00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:25.560
What the hell kind of outfit
gets to choose what orders to accept?

321
00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:27.280
The IMF was expressly created

322
00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:30.520
to ensure there would be
no unintended consequences.

323
00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:33.640
If they cannot ensure
a mission's ultimate outcome

324
00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:36.120
they're authorized to decline.

325
00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:26.920
I understand.

326
00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:28.920
You're upset.

327
00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:31.320
I'm not upset. Kittridge.

328
00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:34.200
You wanted me to listen.

329
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:38.040
This is me listening.

330
00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:40.680
All right.

331
00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:43.000
I put the bounty on Ilsa's head.

332
00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:45.120
I also told you how to find her!

333
00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:47.560
And I didn't ask her
to steal the key.

334
00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:49.880
She did that for reasons of her own.

335
00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:54.000
But that's the pattern. isn't it?

336
00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:00.200
You get her out of trouble
and she always found her way back in.

337
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:11.720
Wait! Ilsa!

338
00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:13.800
Ilsa. wait! It's me!

339
00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:15.600
It's me.

340
00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.200
It's okay.

341
00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:58.040
Listen to me!
You're dead! You stay dead!

342
00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:00.000
Ethan. wait!

343
00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:06.600
I'm not going to apologize
to you. Hunt.

344
00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.680
It's my job to use you.

345
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:11.200
Just like it's your job to be of use.

346
00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:15.200
Did you accomplish
your mission or not?

347
00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:22.000
Wherever the other half of this is

348
00:24:22.400 --> 00:24:24.880
whatever the completed key unlocks

349
00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:26.880
I will find it.

350
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:29.760
And then what?

351
00:24:30.240 --> 00:24:33.640
No one should be trusted
with control of the Entity.

352
00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:36.000
I mean to kill it.

353
00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:37.080
Ethan

354
00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:39.520
the next world war
isn't gonna be a cold one.

355
00:24:39.600 --> 00:24:42.400
It's gonna be a shooting war.
it's gonna be a ballistic war

356
00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:44.400
over a rapidly shrinking ecosystem.

357
00:24:44.480 --> 00:24:47.160
It's gonna be a war
for the last of our dwindling energy

358
00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:49.480
drinkable water. breathable air.

359
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:53.680
Whoever controls the Entity
controls the truth.

360
00:24:54.960 --> 00:24:57.120
The concepts of right and wrong

361
00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:01.120
can be clearly defined for everyone
for centuries to come.

362
00:25:01.400 --> 00:25:03.000
Do you even hear yourself?

363
00:25:03.760 --> 00:25:07.880
Your days of fighting
for the so-called greater good

364
00:25:09.040 --> 00:25:10.160
are over.

365
00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:12.960
You need to pick a side.

366
00:25:13.640 --> 00:25:15.800
I'm on the same side
I've always been on.

367
00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:19.120
Stay out of my way.

368
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.280
I can't do that.

369
00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:23.976
We're gonna be coming after you.

370
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.080
The world's gonna
be coming after you.

371
00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:29.800
And one way or another.
this mission of yours

372
00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:34.320
is gonna cost you dearly.

373
00:25:42.800 --> 00:25:45.400
If I don't get that.
we're gonna have company real soon.

374
00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:02.800
Hello?

375
00:26:02.880 --> 00:26:04.320
<i>Director Denlinger. please.</i>

376
00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:08.360
Director is unavailable
at the moment. How can I help you?

377
00:26:08.440 --> 00:26:09.440
<i>To whom am I speaking?</i>

378
00:26:09.520 --> 00:26:11.480
CIA Director Eugene Kittridge.

379
00:26:11.560 --> 00:26:12.560
<i>Designator?</i>

380
00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:14.280
"Bassnote." lowercase. all one word.

381
00:26:14.360 --> 00:26:16.440
<i>Sir. we have a situation.</i>

382
00:26:16.520 --> 00:26:17.520
No kidding.

383
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:21.320
<i>Your adjutant was found unconscious
in his home ten minutes ago.</i>

384
00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:22.680
<i>It appears he was drugged.</i>

385
00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:24.280
I understand.

386
00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:25.640
<i>I don't think you do. sir.</i>

387
00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:28.920
<i>Security has him entering
this facility 15 minutes ago.</i>

388
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:30.560
I understand. thank you.

389
00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:32.880
<i>Are you able to speak freely?</i>

390
00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:34.160
No. thank you.

391
00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:35.680
<i>A security team is on their way.</i>

392
00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:37.680
<i>If you're in any danger.
simply hang up the phone</i>

393
00:26:37.760 --> 00:26:38.960
<i>before I count to five.</i>

394
00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:40.560
<i>One. two...</i>

395
00:26:44.120 --> 00:26:47.040
So. just how do you plan
on getting out of here?

396
00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:53.640
Of course.

397
00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:01.600
Listen up.

398
00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:04.480
An American operative
with a grievance against his country

399
00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:06.920
is missing and has malfunctioned.

400
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.840
His agenda represents a threat
to our national interests

401
00:28:09.920 --> 00:28:12.280
and he must be neutralized
at all cost.

402
00:28:12.520 --> 00:28:15.480
Anything in this man's possession
is of vital importance

403
00:28:15.560 --> 00:28:17.600
and must be captured intact.

404
00:28:17.680 --> 00:28:20.080
The man himself is expendable.

405
00:28:20.160 --> 00:28:22.320
He is not to be underestimated.

406
00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:26.760
A master of infiltration. deception.
sabotage and psych warfare.

407
00:28:26.920 --> 00:28:29.360
For all intents and purposes.
ladies and gentlemen

408
00:28:29.440 --> 00:28:32.080
a mind-reading. shape-shifting
incarnation of chaos.

409
00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:36.120
So. for your safety
and the safety of those around you

410
00:28:36.600 --> 00:28:38.320
do not consider him secure

411
00:28:38.600 --> 00:28:42.000
unless you have driven a wooden stake
through his open heart.

412
00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:44.400
This is not a drill.

413
00:28:46.160 --> 00:28:51.800
A self-aware. self-learning.
truth-eating digital parasite

414
00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:55.000
infesting all of cyberspace.

415
00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:58.400
Well. it was bound
to happen sooner or later.

416
00:28:58.480 --> 00:29:00.120
And the two halves of this key

417
00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:04.320
just might provide
the means of controlling this Entity.

418
00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:06.120
Meaning every government
on the planet

419
00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:08.080
would kill us just to get that key.

420
00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:10.520
- Including our own.
- Exactly.

421
00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:12.600
Putting us on an unsanctioned mission

422
00:29:12.680 --> 00:29:15.000
which has gone rogue
before it even started.

423
00:29:15.080 --> 00:29:19.960
Meaning this very conversation
is technically an act of treason.

424
00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:23.000
Or as we like to call it. Monday.

425
00:29:25.040 --> 00:29:26.080
So. what's the play?

426
00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:28.960
A buyer's coming in
on Flight 746 from Amsterdam

427
00:29:29.040 --> 00:29:30.280
for a 30-minute layover

428
00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:33.560
at which time he is hoping
to purchase that half of the key.

429
00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:35.880
And it stands to reason
the buyer will have

430
00:29:35.960 --> 00:29:38.000
the other half of the key
somewhere on their person.

431
00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:40.680
Being the only way
to authenticate our half.

432
00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:42.920
So. how do we identify the buyer?

433
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:44.280
This Geiger counter will detect

434
00:29:44.360 --> 00:29:46.320
a radiological signature
of the dragon's egg

435
00:29:46.400 --> 00:29:47.600
embedded in the buyer's key.

436
00:29:47.800 --> 00:29:50.320
The augmented-reality overlay
in these glasses

437
00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:51.800
will lead us to it.

438
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.200
Oh. that's very clever.

439
00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:59.440
So. you ID the buyer.
pick his pockets. Bob's your uncle.

440
00:29:59.520 --> 00:30:01.840
- No.
- No. Of course not.

441
00:30:01.920 --> 00:30:04.640
The complete key is of no value
if we don't know what it unlocks.

442
00:30:04.720 --> 00:30:08.240
So you're going to sell the buyer
our half of the key.

443
00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:10.800
While we figure out
the buyer's connecting flight

444
00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:12.760
and book you a seat on that plane.

445
00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:15.680
So you can follow the key
wherever it goes.

446
00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:18.800
Which you hope is into the hands
of someone who knows what it unlocks.

447
00:30:18.880 --> 00:30:19.920
Precisely.

448
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:21.760
Finding the completed key

449
00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:24.040
is only the beginning.

450
00:30:24.120 --> 00:30:28.760
The fate of the world depends
on finding whatever it unlocks.

451
00:30:32.200 --> 00:30:34.280
This guy. you know him?

452
00:30:35.600 --> 00:30:36.800
Not personally.

453
00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:38.880
But it is personal.

454
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:09.000
Thank you.

455
00:31:15.400 --> 00:31:16.520
- Hey. what's that?
- What?

456
00:31:16.600 --> 00:31:19.600
Security alert.
Suspicious bag on its way to Venice.

457
00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:22.000
Nope. it's gone.
Must have been a false alarm.

458
00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:32.400
Overwatch. Snap Shot. Where's he at?

459
00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:37.920
Snap Shot. Overwatch. I have him.

460
00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:40.320
Terminal B. Gate 15. headed south.

461
00:31:42.920 --> 00:31:44.560
- I am so.
- You are not.

462
00:31:45.400 --> 00:31:48.160
Ethan. would you care to explain
to our friend. the Net Ranger

463
00:31:48.240 --> 00:31:50.120
<i>how I am just as capable
of writing code</i>

464
00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:51.280
- <i>as he is?</i>
- No comment.

465
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:52.920
What. you figure Phineas Phreak here

466
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:55.176
is gonna single-handedly work out
a way to kill the Entity

467
00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:57.040
<i>while I just hold his soldering iron?</i>

468
00:31:57.120 --> 00:31:58.880
- Probably.
- Definitely.

469
00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:00.800
Out of the way!

470
00:32:02.280 --> 00:32:03.320
Tell me where he is.

471
00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:05.000
- <i>Where is he?</i>
- Blue suit.

472
00:32:05.280 --> 00:32:06.320
Right in front of you.

473
00:32:16.720 --> 00:32:22.880
(Italian)

474
00:32:24.400 --> 00:32:27.200
(Italian)

475
00:32:29.920 --> 00:32:31.240
(Italian)

476
00:32:31.320 --> 00:32:32.800
- It's not him.
- It's him.

477
00:32:32.880 --> 00:32:33.976
<i>I'm telling you. it's not him.</i>

478
00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:37.200
And I'm telling you.
facial comes back with a perfect...

479
00:32:41.240 --> 00:32:42.480
How did you do that?

480
00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:45.320
No one is safe from Phineas Phreak.

481
00:32:53.040 --> 00:32:54.640
- I got him!
- <i>Where is he?</i>

482
00:32:54.840 --> 00:32:56.080
Terminal E. Gate 5.

483
00:32:56.320 --> 00:32:58.680
Goddamn it. that's clear
on the other side of the airport.

484
00:33:01.920 --> 00:33:03.920
<i>Ethan. they're headed to Terminal E.</i>

485
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.840
<i>That side of the airport
is all yours.</i>

486
00:33:07.320 --> 00:33:09.520
- Thank you. Luther. I see the buyer.
- <i>Got him.</i>

487
00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:12.480
The buyer is Otto Von Bork.
Swiss national.

488
00:33:12.640 --> 00:33:16.800
<i>He's connecting to Venice. departing
in 30 minutes on Flight 1031.</i>

489
00:33:16.880 --> 00:33:18.376
Benji. get me
on that flight to Venice.

490
00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:20.880
Yep. Flight 1031 to Venice. Stand by.

491
00:33:31.480 --> 00:33:32.480
What?

492
00:33:33.240 --> 00:33:34.920
<i>Ethan. what just happened?</i>

493
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:36.280
- He was bumped.
- <i>Bumped?</i>

494
00:33:36.360 --> 00:33:37.720
What do you mean. bumped?

495
00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:39.760
<i>That woman picked
his pocket. Tag her.</i>

496
00:33:39.840 --> 00:33:40.840
Tell me who she is.

497
00:33:49.560 --> 00:33:50.680
Luther. mute our comms.

498
00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:52.896
- What is it?
- That bag was on its way

499
00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:54.600
- to Flight 1031.
- What bag?

500
00:33:54.680 --> 00:33:57.200
There was a suspicious bag alert
a few minutes ago.

501
00:33:57.280 --> 00:34:00.000
- So what about it?
- It was on its way to Flight 1031.

502
00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:02.080
To Venice. It's the buyer's plane.

503
00:34:02.160 --> 00:34:03.320
It's Ethan's plane.

504
00:34:03.800 --> 00:34:05.400
Luther. do you copy? Who is she?

505
00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:06.856
What if it wasn't a false alarm?

506
00:34:06.880 --> 00:34:09.320
What if somebody's trying to smuggle
a bomb onto that plane?

507
00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:11.600
And what if that's what
the Entity wants us to think

508
00:34:11.680 --> 00:34:12.920
to keep Ethan off that plane?

509
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:14.920
- <i>Luther. what's happening?</i>
- Should we warn him?

510
00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:17.400
- No.
<i>- Guys...? You hear me?</i>

511
00:34:17.480 --> 00:34:19.920
Find that bag. I'll direct you. Go.

512
00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:22.480
<i>Luther. just tell me.
is there something wrong?</i>

513
00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:25.360
Nothing to worry about.
It's under control.

514
00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:29.160
Got her. Info on the woman
is coming... now.

515
00:34:32.760 --> 00:34:36.000
<i>Whoever she is. she's no spy.</i>

516
00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:37.560
She's a thief.

517
00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:39.400
<i>Where am I going. Luther?</i>

518
00:34:39.480 --> 00:34:41.520
Benji. there's a door
on your immediate left.

519
00:34:42.200 --> 00:34:43.640
<i>I'm unlocking it now.</i>

520
00:34:47.320 --> 00:34:50.320
The bag you're after is on tray 01833

521
00:34:50.400 --> 00:34:53.000
<i>heading towards
the northwest corner of the facility.</i>

522
00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:54.200
Copy that!

523
00:35:04.880 --> 00:35:05.880
Hi.

524
00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:09.120
Hello.

525
00:35:13.080 --> 00:35:14.120
Oh. I get it.

526
00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:16.640
You thought I was someone else.

527
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:20.040
I'm not interested.

528
00:35:21.560 --> 00:35:22.640
Give me a chance.

529
00:35:23.720 --> 00:35:24.720
I'll scream.

530
00:35:26.360 --> 00:35:27.360
Please do.

531
00:35:30.560 --> 00:35:31.680
What do you want?

532
00:35:32.960 --> 00:35:33.960
This key.

533
00:35:35.640 --> 00:35:37.560
The one you picked
from that man's pocket.

534
00:35:38.080 --> 00:35:39.120
It's worthless

535
00:35:39.680 --> 00:35:40.680
without this key.

536
00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:44.000
But together

537
00:35:44.400 --> 00:35:46.056
they're worth four million
in cryptocurrency

538
00:35:46.080 --> 00:35:47.720
that man was carrying on
a flash drive.

539
00:35:49.840 --> 00:35:51.480
Well. I wouldn't know
anything about that.

540
00:35:51.520 --> 00:35:53.080
Then. why was this drive
in your pocket?

541
00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:56.400
Who are you?

542
00:35:56.640 --> 00:35:57.800
You working with someone?

543
00:35:58.600 --> 00:36:00.680
Never. I'm strictly single-0.

544
00:36:01.120 --> 00:36:02.160
Today you got a partner.

545
00:36:02.920 --> 00:36:03.976
I need the man you stole this from

546
00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.880
to complete a transaction and
leave this airport with both of these

547
00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:08.536
without ever knowing
his pocket was picked

548
00:36:08.560 --> 00:36:09.816
and before he boards his flight in...

549
00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:11.040
<i>Seven minutes.</i>

550
00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:12.280
Seven minutes.

551
00:36:13.160 --> 00:36:15.040
We both know
you're a good pickpocket.

552
00:36:15.640 --> 00:36:17.320
Let's see
what kind of put-pocket you are.

553
00:36:19.080 --> 00:36:21.640
You expect me to put it back.

554
00:36:22.080 --> 00:36:23.320
Oh. I know you will.

555
00:36:23.800 --> 00:36:26.040
You're a thief. You want the money.

556
00:36:26.120 --> 00:36:27.320
And I can give it to you.

557
00:36:28.560 --> 00:36:29.720
Your choice.

558
00:36:30.760 --> 00:36:32.160
You're in or you're out.

559
00:36:34.480 --> 00:36:35.480
All right.

560
00:36:36.120 --> 00:36:37.120
So. what's the play?

561
00:36:37.200 --> 00:36:39.160
<i>I sure hope you know
what you're doing.</i>

562
00:36:39.720 --> 00:36:40.720
After you.

563
00:36:43.040 --> 00:36:45.120
Oh. I won't be needing this.

564
00:36:45.640 --> 00:36:47.000
I don't smoke.

565
00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:49.120
Keep it.

566
00:36:49.440 --> 00:36:50.960
Something to remember me by.

567
00:36:56.080 --> 00:36:59.080
<i>Ethan. the alloy
in that key she took off the buyer</i>

568
00:36:59.160 --> 00:37:01.160
doesn't match. It's counterfeit.

569
00:37:01.240 --> 00:37:02.760
I expect nothing less.

570
00:37:02.840 --> 00:37:04.320
<i>But that doesn't change
our objective.</i>

571
00:37:04.400 --> 00:37:05.880
<i>The buyer has to leave
with both keys.</i>

572
00:37:05.960 --> 00:37:07.760
<i>Talk to me. Luther! Where am I going?</i>

573
00:37:07.840 --> 00:37:09.640
Benji. head down the stairs
in front of you

574
00:37:09.720 --> 00:37:11.016
and the bag should be right there.

575
00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:12.520
Okay. I'm there. I'm there.

576
00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:19.000
That's him.

577
00:37:19.280 --> 00:37:20.360
<i>Right in front of you.</i>

578
00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:23.880
Okay... Hey... Sorry...

579
00:37:23.960 --> 00:37:25.200
Thought you were somebody else.

580
00:37:26.920 --> 00:37:28.760
Hunt's jerking our chain.

581
00:37:29.520 --> 00:37:32.240
Everybody! Two-man teams. spread out.

582
00:37:32.320 --> 00:37:34.880
Ethan. our American friends
are getting wise.

583
00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:36.800
They're breaking up
and canvassing the airport.

584
00:37:36.840 --> 00:37:38.120
<i>Keep your eyes peeled.</i>

585
00:37:38.200 --> 00:37:39.400
So. what do I call you?

586
00:37:39.920 --> 00:37:42.200
How about Grace? And you?

587
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:43.520
Well. listen. Grace.

588
00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:45.776
You should know
we're not the only interested party.

589
00:37:45.800 --> 00:37:47.600
If I tell you to run. you run.

590
00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:48.680
Run?

591
00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:50.520
This is getting exciting.

592
00:37:51.160 --> 00:37:52.560
Benji. have you got that bag?

593
00:37:52.640 --> 00:37:53.720
I found it...!

594
00:38:07.120 --> 00:38:10.960
<i>There's a cylindrical device inside.
I'm... I'm gonna take it out.</i>

595
00:38:15.040 --> 00:38:16.040
<i>How we doing. Luther?</i>

596
00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:18.920
Ethan. the buyer's
in the waiting area above you.

597
00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:20.680
<i>Top of the escalator.</i>

598
00:38:22.640 --> 00:38:24.360
<i>All units are headed
in your direction.</i>

599
00:38:24.520 --> 00:38:27.520
<i>Your location is going to be crawling
with agents anytime now.</i>

600
00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:38.320
Whatever it is.
I've just activated it.

601
00:38:40.920 --> 00:38:42.760
Looks like we have five minutes.

602
00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:47.000
- <i>Also. it appears to be nuclear.</i>
- How big?

603
00:38:47.080 --> 00:38:48.816
Big enough to matter
to everybody in this airport

604
00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:50.120
- I suspect.
- Can you disarm it?

605
00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:51.400
I haven't got any tools!

606
00:38:51.480 --> 00:38:52.480
<i>Then find some.</i>

607
00:38:52.560 --> 00:38:53.640
Where am I gonna find...

608
00:39:16.880 --> 00:39:18.120
Is this where we run?

609
00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:20.000
Not yet.

610
00:39:20.760 --> 00:39:22.560
Benji. how are you doing
with that bomb?

611
00:39:22.640 --> 00:39:23.640
Come on...

612
00:39:25.200 --> 00:39:26.200
I got it!

613
00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:30.280
It... It's a cylinder cypher.
There's eight wheels.

614
00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:32.400
Looks like 14 letters on each wheel.

615
00:39:32.480 --> 00:39:35.120
1.5 billion possible combinations.

616
00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:36.280
Give or take.

617
00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:38.720
Oh. my God.

618
00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:39.800
<i>What now?</i>

619
00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.680
The wheels...
They spell out a message.

620
00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:44.960
- U.R.DUNN.
- <i>No way.</i>

621
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:46.600
- Not yet. we aren't.
- <i>No... Luther</i>

622
00:39:46.680 --> 00:39:47.920
not D-O-N-E.

623
00:39:48.160 --> 00:39:50.200
D-U-N-N.

624
00:39:50.720 --> 00:39:52.160
It's my last name.

625
00:39:56.320 --> 00:39:57.440
It knows who I am.

626
00:40:09.960 --> 00:40:11.600
Hold on. There's a message
on the display.

627
00:40:11.960 --> 00:40:13.480
<i>"I speak without a mouth</i>

628
00:40:13.680 --> 00:40:15.760
I fly through the air without wings.

629
00:40:15.840 --> 00:40:17.200
- What am I?"
- You got me. What?

630
00:40:17.280 --> 00:40:19.960
No. It's a riddle. I suspect
this thing is voice-activated.

631
00:40:20.040 --> 00:40:21.240
It wants me to say the answer.

632
00:40:21.520 --> 00:40:22.920
"I fly through the air..."

633
00:40:23.360 --> 00:40:24.400
An echo!

634
00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:26.720
That's it...!

635
00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:27.960
Okay. new message.

636
00:40:28.040 --> 00:40:30.520
"Are you afraid of death?"

637
00:40:30.720 --> 00:40:32.800
- What kind of a riddle is that?
- <i>It's not a riddle.</i>

638
00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:34.680
It's a psychometric test.

639
00:40:35.040 --> 00:40:38.960
The more questions you answer.
the more it'll know about you.

640
00:40:39.040 --> 00:40:40.520
"Are you afraid of death?" No!

641
00:40:42.080 --> 00:40:43.160
<i>Did it work?</i>

642
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:44.640
I lied. It knows.

643
00:40:44.720 --> 00:40:46.800
Just tell it the truth. Say it.

644
00:40:47.160 --> 00:40:49.520
"Are you afraid of death?"
Yes! Who isn't?

645
00:40:59.160 --> 00:41:02.200
Okay. "What's always approaching
but never arrives?"

646
00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:03.960
Wait... I know this one.

647
00:41:04.040 --> 00:41:05.360
The clock is ticking. Luther.

648
00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:07.416
Riddles aren't my thing. Benji.
What more can I say?

649
00:41:07.440 --> 00:41:08.800
We're running out of time!

650
00:41:09.920 --> 00:41:10.920
There he is.

651
00:41:11.400 --> 00:41:12.720
Oh. this is too easy.

652
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:15.680
<i>Sorry to bother you. Ethan.
Would you happen to know</i>

653
00:41:15.760 --> 00:41:17.400
what's always approaching

654
00:41:17.880 --> 00:41:19.200
but never arrives?

655
00:41:19.280 --> 00:41:21.400
What is always approaching
but never arrives?

656
00:41:21.680 --> 00:41:22.680
Tomorrow.

657
00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:25.120
- What?
- Always approaching

658
00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:26.280
but never arrives.

659
00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:27.360
Tomorrow.

660
00:41:27.760 --> 00:41:28.920
- It's tomorrow.
- Tomorrow.

661
00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:30.440
Tomorrow...!

662
00:41:30.520 --> 00:41:32.200
Yes! Okay. next question.

663
00:41:32.440 --> 00:41:33.440
Give me the goods.

664
00:41:34.240 --> 00:41:35.280
I'll be watching.

665
00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:36.520
You don't trust me?

666
00:41:42.200 --> 00:41:43.600
Luther. what is happening?

667
00:41:43.680 --> 00:41:45.200
Nothing to worry about. Every...

668
00:41:45.280 --> 00:41:46.720
<i>Everything is under control.</i>

669
00:41:46.800 --> 00:41:48.520
Okay. next question. "Who or what

670
00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:50.800
is the most important thing to you?"

671
00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:52.680
- Say it.
- I can... But if I...

672
00:41:52.760 --> 00:41:54.080
There's no other choice. Say it.

673
00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:56.120
My friends.

674
00:41:57.200 --> 00:41:58.200
Bastard.

675
00:42:09.320 --> 00:42:11.080
- Is he...
- Yes. he is.

676
00:42:11.280 --> 00:42:12.760
Give me the money. give me the key.

677
00:42:14.080 --> 00:42:16.880
Okay... "What gets bigger
the more you take away?"

678
00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:18.800
- A hole.
- A hole! Brilliant...!

679
00:42:30.520 --> 00:42:32.536
I've got no more questions
and there's one more wheel.

680
00:42:32.560 --> 00:42:34.576
How am I supposed to give answers
if I've got no questions?

681
00:42:34.600 --> 00:42:35.880
That must be your final test.

682
00:42:35.960 --> 00:42:37.720
I've got 45 seconds!

683
00:42:40.840 --> 00:42:41.880
What happens now?

684
00:42:42.280 --> 00:42:44.160
I'm thinking. Don't move.

685
00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:46.840
Listen. I'm pinned down. Need a way
out of here. Where am I going?

686
00:42:46.960 --> 00:42:49.120
We have a bigger problem. Ethan.
It's very possible

687
00:42:49.200 --> 00:42:50.880
- no one is getting out of here.
- What?

688
00:42:50.960 --> 00:42:53.760
There's a bomb in baggage handling.
A nuclear bomb.

689
00:42:53.840 --> 00:42:56.320
<i>The question I asked you
is part of the code for disarming it.</i>

690
00:42:56.400 --> 00:42:57.680
Stop...!

691
00:42:59.880 --> 00:43:01.000
Why didn't you tell me this?

692
00:43:01.200 --> 00:43:03.056
Well. you had a lot going on.
We didn't want to bother you.

693
00:43:03.080 --> 00:43:04.600
Listen to me. A nuclear bomb

694
00:43:04.680 --> 00:43:06.680
is something
you bother me with immediately.

695
00:43:06.760 --> 00:43:08.200
- How much time?
- 20 seconds.

696
00:43:09.040 --> 00:43:10.040
- 20 seconds?
- <i>Wait.</i>

697
00:43:10.120 --> 00:43:12.280
There's one more riddle.
I'm working on it. 15 seconds!

698
00:43:12.360 --> 00:43:14.280
Easy... What's the riddle?

699
00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:15.656
In the time it takes me to explain

700
00:43:15.680 --> 00:43:16.936
- we're all gonna be dead!
- Come on. Benji.

701
00:43:16.960 --> 00:43:19.120
Why do we always
end up in these situations?

702
00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:20.440
<i>Ten seconds.</i>

703
00:43:20.720 --> 00:43:22.120
<i>Nine. eight</i>

704
00:43:22.440 --> 00:43:25.400
seven. six. five...

705
00:43:36.200 --> 00:43:38.080
- <i>Oh. my God.</i>
- What is it?

706
00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:40.840
It's empty.

707
00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:43.400
- What do you mean. empty?
- <i>There's nothing inside.</i>

708
00:43:48.800 --> 00:43:49.800
She took the key.

709
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:51.600
- Which key?
- Our key. The real key.

710
00:43:51.680 --> 00:43:52.760
- What?
- <i>Luther. find her.</i>

711
00:44:02.600 --> 00:44:04.200
I got her.
She's headed for Terminal E.

712
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:18.040
- No. it can't be.
- What is it?

713
00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:20.040
Luther. Benji. Abort... Get out!

714
00:44:20.120 --> 00:44:22.080
- Where do we rendezvous?
- No. we don't!

715
00:44:22.160 --> 00:44:24.800
This mission is terminated.
Get out now.

716
00:44:35.880 --> 00:44:38.120
Hunt! Hey. stop right there! Hey!

717
00:44:38.520 --> 00:44:40.280
You see him...? Where is he?

718
00:44:40.720 --> 00:44:42.120
Excuse me! Excuse me!

719
00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:44.440
Sorry...!

720
00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:22.240
- Move!
- Move...!

721
00:46:02.800 --> 00:46:04.520
He's got to be here somewhere.

722
00:46:05.920 --> 00:46:07.400
Goddamn.

723
00:46:17.880 --> 00:46:20.200
What we have here is shortwave radio

724
00:46:20.280 --> 00:46:24.280
magnetic audio recording.
cathode ray tube monitors.

725
00:46:24.920 --> 00:46:26.800
No more ones and zeros.

726
00:46:27.360 --> 00:46:30.160
It's a fully analog.
offline safe room

727
00:46:30.240 --> 00:46:32.720
shielded from
our digitally-based Entity.

728
00:46:34.400 --> 00:46:36.240
Where is this feed coming from?

729
00:46:36.320 --> 00:46:38.840
CORONA spy satellite
from the Cold War.

730
00:46:39.960 --> 00:46:41.880
Had no idea we were still
using those things.

731
00:46:41.960 --> 00:46:43.160
Yeah. well. we weren't.

732
00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:45.736
Gave them to the National
Weather Service 20 years ago.

733
00:46:45.760 --> 00:46:47.760
This is the last one
still functioning.

734
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:51.760
So. will this thing help us find
your nameless IMF man?

735
00:46:51.920 --> 00:46:53.680
Nothing can do that. sir.

736
00:46:53.760 --> 00:46:57.240
But it has allowed us
to keep tabs on this woman.

737
00:46:59.040 --> 00:47:01.800
She was seen with our man
at the airport in Abu Dhabi.

738
00:47:02.880 --> 00:47:03.880
Who is she?

739
00:47:04.960 --> 00:47:06.360
Where is she now?

740
00:47:17.520 --> 00:47:21.000
You are here because Italian police
received an anonymous tip

741
00:47:21.160 --> 00:47:23.080
that a woman
matching your description

742
00:47:23.240 --> 00:47:26.320
would be arriving on
the afternoon flight from Abu Dhabi.

743
00:47:26.600 --> 00:47:30.080
This woman had
multiple passports in her possession.

744
00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:34.000
This one is wanted for fraud
in Saint Petersburg.

745
00:47:34.680 --> 00:47:36.360
Jewel theft in Antwerp.

746
00:47:36.440 --> 00:47:37.800
Art theft in Monaco.

747
00:47:37.880 --> 00:47:40.680
Graft in Milan. Extortion in Mumbai.

748
00:47:41.080 --> 00:47:43.480
But this is my favorite

749
00:47:43.560 --> 00:47:45.520
resisting arrest in Rio.

750
00:47:47.800 --> 00:47:49.520
Which leads me to wonder

751
00:47:50.680 --> 00:47:52.240
which one of these women is you?

752
00:47:53.320 --> 00:47:55.200
I've never seen these
before in my life.

753
00:47:55.600 --> 00:47:56.720
They were in your purse.

754
00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:59.600
And your picture is in every one.

755
00:47:59.960 --> 00:48:01.760
- May I see?
- Please.

756
00:48:07.280 --> 00:48:08.840
Yes. it's an amazing likeness

757
00:48:08.920 --> 00:48:10.680
but it isn't me.

758
00:48:11.800 --> 00:48:13.200
As I keep telling you. I'm a...

759
00:48:14.400 --> 00:48:17.000
I'm a schoolteacher from Brighton.
I'm on a sabbatical.

760
00:48:17.720 --> 00:48:19.320
Whatever you're involved in

761
00:48:19.600 --> 00:48:23.000
you've obviously made
some very powerful enemies.

762
00:48:31.560 --> 00:48:32.560
<i>Sì.</i>

763
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:34.560
Okay.

764
00:48:37.840 --> 00:48:38.840
Her lawyer is here.

765
00:48:39.440 --> 00:48:40.480
My lawyer?

766
00:49:14.520 --> 00:49:16.200
Magistrate Spezzi.

767
00:49:17.080 --> 00:49:18.200
I'm sorry. Who are you?

768
00:49:18.840 --> 00:49:19.880
Interpol.

769
00:49:21.280 --> 00:49:25.240
I've come regarding the arrest
of the woman from Abu Dhabi.

770
00:49:25.840 --> 00:49:28.800
I'll need to inventory the items on
her person at the time of her arrest.

771
00:49:29.600 --> 00:49:31.600
May I see
some identification. please?

772
00:49:32.680 --> 00:49:33.680
Where's the rest?

773
00:49:34.200 --> 00:49:36.000
I assure you. this is everything.

774
00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:38.320
- What was your name?
- She left Abu Dhabi

775
00:49:38.400 --> 00:49:39.440
with a certain key.

776
00:49:39.920 --> 00:49:41.120
There was no key.

777
00:49:41.200 --> 00:49:42.880
It was an unusual sort.

778
00:49:44.160 --> 00:49:46.160
One that you could mistake
for a pendant.

779
00:49:47.120 --> 00:49:49.920
The kind that you'd be tempted
to hang on a chain

780
00:49:50.560 --> 00:49:52.000
around Amelia's neck.

781
00:49:53.800 --> 00:49:54.800
Amelia?

782
00:49:55.720 --> 00:49:56.760
Your wife.

783
00:49:57.560 --> 00:50:00.000
Mother of your lovely daughter.
Serena.

784
00:50:00.600 --> 00:50:02.040
You're not Interpol.

785
00:50:02.400 --> 00:50:04.280
I am if I wish to be.

786
00:50:05.360 --> 00:50:08.200
I can be anything.
and I know everything.

787
00:50:08.840 --> 00:50:10.136
I know this wouldn't
be the first time

788
00:50:10.160 --> 00:50:12.120
you've helped yourself
to stolen goods.

789
00:50:12.200 --> 00:50:13.680
A Cartier bracelet.

790
00:50:14.080 --> 00:50:15.600
You were cleared of suspicion

791
00:50:15.680 --> 00:50:18.000
but we both know you gave it
to your mistress. Valeria.

792
00:50:18.400 --> 00:50:21.400
On August 21st. Her 29th birthday.

793
00:50:21.880 --> 00:50:23.600
Who are you?

794
00:50:25.520 --> 00:50:27.320
I'm gonna have to search you

795
00:50:27.840 --> 00:50:28.840
just to be sure.

796
00:50:29.720 --> 00:50:30.720
(Italian)

797
00:50:32.960 --> 00:50:35.200
Your secretary's no longer with us.

798
00:51:12.280 --> 00:51:13.320
You.

799
00:51:14.040 --> 00:51:15.240
You did this.

800
00:51:15.320 --> 00:51:19.560
I called the police. I didn't
tell them about your colorful past.

801
00:51:21.080 --> 00:51:22.120
That's on you.

802
00:51:23.120 --> 00:51:26.520
You put-pocketed that key on another
passenger before you were arrested.

803
00:51:26.840 --> 00:51:29.720
You exchanged details
and arranged to meet later on.

804
00:51:29.800 --> 00:51:32.280
Right now someone out there
hasn't the slightest clue

805
00:51:32.360 --> 00:51:33.880
they're holding on
to that key for you.

806
00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:36.080
An unwitting courier.

807
00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:37.760
The perfect accomplice.

808
00:51:38.440 --> 00:51:41.040
I'm guessing a man middle-aged?

809
00:51:41.760 --> 00:51:45.600
A man waiting his whole life
to be noticed by a woman like you.

810
00:51:47.440 --> 00:51:48.440
An orphan.

811
00:51:49.760 --> 00:51:52.760
Highly intelligent.
Inherently resourceful.

812
00:51:53.160 --> 00:51:56.480
Growing up in poverty left you
longing for the finer things.

813
00:51:57.240 --> 00:51:58.800
Other people's things.

814
00:51:59.480 --> 00:52:02.920
Someone saw your potential
and helped you hone your skills.

815
00:52:03.520 --> 00:52:05.960
Skills that gave you
the life you thought you wanted.

816
00:52:06.040 --> 00:52:09.160
Tailored clothes.
fine dining. luxury hotels.

817
00:52:09.520 --> 00:52:12.200
Skills that kept you
one step ahead of the law

818
00:52:13.200 --> 00:52:14.360
until now.

819
00:52:16.360 --> 00:52:19.120
You can't blame a girl for
trying to make a dishonest living.

820
00:52:20.320 --> 00:52:23.000
You had no idea
what you were stealing.

821
00:52:23.080 --> 00:52:25.040
Otherwise you never
would have stolen it.

822
00:52:26.240 --> 00:52:27.240
Tell you what.

823
00:52:27.560 --> 00:52:30.200
You get me out of here. and
I'll take you straight to the key.

824
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:32.000
I have a better idea.

825
00:52:32.280 --> 00:52:33.880
You're gonna tell me everything.

826
00:52:34.240 --> 00:52:36.040
Then I'll think
about getting you out of here.

827
00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:37.880
Now start with who hired you.

828
00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:40.840
And don't lie to me.
because I'll know.

829
00:52:40.920 --> 00:52:42.640
I have no idea who hired me.

830
00:52:42.720 --> 00:52:44.960
Contact with the client
was almost entirely electronic.

831
00:52:45.040 --> 00:52:46.040
- Email?
- Texts.

832
00:52:46.120 --> 00:52:47.280
- Encrypted?
- Naturally.

833
00:52:47.440 --> 00:52:48.520
- Almost?
- Pardon?

834
00:52:48.600 --> 00:52:51.600
You said contact with the client
was "almost" entirely electronic.

835
00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:54.320
There was a dead drop
in a café in Luxembourg.

836
00:52:54.400 --> 00:52:56.016
- An envelope.
- What was in the envelope?

837
00:52:56.040 --> 00:52:57.680
A ticket to Abu Dhabi.

838
00:52:58.800 --> 00:52:59.880
And...

839
00:53:00.560 --> 00:53:03.200
a picture of you.

840
00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:06.880
My instructions were
to follow you at the airport.

841
00:53:07.000 --> 00:53:08.240
You'd be tailing a mark.

842
00:53:08.320 --> 00:53:11.200
Said mark would have a key
and four million in cryptocurrency.

843
00:53:11.440 --> 00:53:13.600
That drive was useless.
by the way. It was empty.

844
00:53:14.400 --> 00:53:17.280
The only hope I have of getting paid
is to deliver your half of the key.

845
00:53:17.360 --> 00:53:19.720
And you were instructed
to deliver it to...

846
00:53:19.800 --> 00:53:20.800
Venice.

847
00:53:20.880 --> 00:53:23.400
Party at Ducale Palace.
Tomorrow. Midnight.

848
00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:27.960
You expecting someone?

849
00:53:28.280 --> 00:53:29.600
Your friends from the airport.

850
00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:31.680
Saw them in the hallway
a few minutes ago.

851
00:53:34.040 --> 00:53:35.800
You could have said something sooner.

852
00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.200
Well. they were chasing you. not me.

853
00:53:59.880 --> 00:54:01.520
A <i>pervertito!</i>

854
00:54:03.440 --> 00:54:04.720
No. Grace...

855
00:54:06.960 --> 00:54:07.960
No...

856
00:54:10.720 --> 00:54:11.720
<i>Grazie.</i>

857
00:54:12.080 --> 00:54:13.080
No. Grace.

858
00:54:18.440 --> 00:54:19.440
No...

859
00:54:21.080 --> 00:54:22.760
<i>Tranquillo...</i>

860
00:54:44.600 --> 00:54:46.600
(Italian)

861
00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:52.960
No...! Move...!

862
00:54:56.200 --> 00:54:57.200
Sorry!

863
00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:14.520
Who parks like that?

864
00:55:32.400 --> 00:55:33.400
Grace!

865
00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:34.800
Grace. You gotta pull over.

866
00:55:35.320 --> 00:55:36.840
Grace. Pull over. Listen.

867
00:55:36.920 --> 00:55:38.800
I'm trying to help you! Grace!

868
00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:17.120
Are you okay?

869
00:56:17.520 --> 00:56:18.760
You okay? No...

870
00:56:25.480 --> 00:56:26.520
Give me your hand.

871
00:56:26.720 --> 00:56:27.760
Slow...

872
00:56:28.560 --> 00:56:29.560
It's okay.

873
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:31.000
Slow.

874
00:56:31.360 --> 00:56:33.640
Is anything broken?
Are you okay? You okay?

875
00:56:33.720 --> 00:56:34.720
Hunt!

876
00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:36.640
It's over!

877
00:56:37.360 --> 00:56:38.520
Let the girl go.

878
00:56:39.160 --> 00:56:40.200
Put the bracelets on.

879
00:56:41.560 --> 00:56:44.480
There you go. Put them on. Do it!

880
00:56:45.040 --> 00:56:46.880
It's okay. He's not gonna shoot you.

881
00:56:55.520 --> 00:56:56.576
(Italian) He's wanted for terrorism.

882
00:56:56.600 --> 00:56:57.656
Goddamn it. Degas.
get rid of those women.

883
00:56:57.680 --> 00:56:58.856
(Italian) Ladies!
Move. all of you get out of here!

884
00:56:58.880 --> 00:57:01.200
- Hunt. listen to me...
- (Italian)

885
00:57:01.280 --> 00:57:02.336
Let her go and put them on.

886
00:57:02.360 --> 00:57:04.200
(Italian)

887
00:57:06.760 --> 00:57:09.120
It's okay...!

888
00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:14.440
No! Everybody down! Down! Get down!

889
00:57:19.400 --> 00:57:22.000
- Down...!
- Cover...!

890
00:57:51.360 --> 00:57:52.800
- You're driving.
- What?

891
00:57:53.280 --> 00:57:54.280
No...!

892
00:57:55.880 --> 00:57:57.160
Go... Hit the accelerator.

893
00:57:57.240 --> 00:57:58.520
Go...!

894
00:58:07.600 --> 00:58:08.640
Go...!

895
00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:26.240
Get in!

896
00:58:26.800 --> 00:58:28.376
You're good.
Just keep it going. keep it going.

897
00:58:28.400 --> 00:58:29.400
Don't stop...

898
00:58:39.360 --> 00:58:40.360
Car...

899
00:58:48.560 --> 00:58:50.841
It's okay. Just put your foot
on the brake. Start the car.

900
00:58:51.760 --> 00:58:52.840
Wait....! What...

901
00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:53.920
What... What's happening?

902
00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:55.360
I'm done. I'm not doing this.

903
00:58:55.440 --> 00:58:57.080
People are chasing us.

904
00:58:57.160 --> 00:58:59.000
Yes. they are. You're driving.

905
00:58:59.080 --> 00:59:00.080
Now. come on.

906
00:59:30.080 --> 00:59:31.480
Who is that person?

907
00:59:32.120 --> 00:59:33.200
I have no idea.

908
00:59:37.840 --> 00:59:39.840
- You okay?
- I will be when this is over.

909
00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:43.680
Oh. man.

910
00:59:47.680 --> 00:59:48.760
It's okay...

911
01:00:01.280 --> 01:00:02.760
Is there anyone not chasing us?

912
01:00:03.440 --> 01:00:04.640
We gotta get rid of this car.

913
01:00:07.160 --> 01:00:08.680
Scooters! Damn it.

914
01:00:29.640 --> 01:00:30.760
What are we doing?

915
01:00:32.960 --> 01:00:34.120
Finding us a new car.

916
01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:56.360
Okay.

917
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:14.240
- Just give me a second.
- Yeah.

918
01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:16.200
- Thanks. Okay?
- Yeah.

919
01:01:16.280 --> 01:01:17.640
- You ready?
- I'm ready.

920
01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:23.000
- Wow.
- You okay?

921
01:01:23.920 --> 01:01:25.800
Yeah. look.
I'm... I'm sorry. This is...

922
01:01:26.120 --> 01:01:27.880
- It's okay.
- No. this car. the way they...

923
01:01:28.400 --> 01:01:29.816
- It's okay.
- No. the way they set them up

924
01:01:29.840 --> 01:01:30.840
sometimes it's just...

925
01:01:30.920 --> 01:01:32.600
- Let's go...
- It takes me...

926
01:02:02.480 --> 01:02:04.800
Now I got you.

927
01:02:13.360 --> 01:02:14.440
Looks like we lost them.

928
01:02:39.520 --> 01:02:40.520
Let's just...

929
01:02:40.600 --> 01:02:41.600
Move...!

930
01:02:58.000 --> 01:02:59.520
Baby...!

931
01:03:11.960 --> 01:03:13.000
Wait. what?

932
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:15.000
No...

933
01:03:20.720 --> 01:03:21.720
Go...!

934
01:03:25.000 --> 01:03:26.000
Go straight.

935
01:03:33.480 --> 01:03:34.536
- Just take your foot off
- We're on fire.

936
01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:35.856
- The accelerator. No...!
- We're on fire!

937
01:03:35.880 --> 01:03:37.880
No...! It's the tires.
Just try to go straight.

938
01:03:39.840 --> 01:03:41.440
- Hang on...
- Why is it spinning?

939
01:03:43.280 --> 01:03:44.320
Good...!

940
01:03:46.920 --> 01:03:48.400
- I've got it...
- Just go straight.

941
01:03:49.920 --> 01:03:51.120
Turn right... Down there.

942
01:03:51.200 --> 01:03:52.520
- Get... Right down...
- Come on!

943
01:04:00.640 --> 01:04:01.840
Got to go right. Turn right!

944
01:04:04.480 --> 01:04:05.696
- Who's driving? Maybe
- You're driving

945
01:04:05.720 --> 01:04:06.776
- you should take your hands off.
- You're driving!

946
01:04:06.800 --> 01:04:08.240
Go...
Just go straight. go straight.

947
01:04:09.160 --> 01:04:10.160
Go...

948
01:04:10.240 --> 01:04:12.040
Just keep going straight.
keep going straight.

949
01:04:12.800 --> 01:04:15.840
Or left.... Go...
You're doing good.

950
01:04:21.680 --> 01:04:23.000
Cops...! A lot of cops!

951
01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:25.600
Take the wheel...

952
01:04:25.680 --> 01:04:26.680
Brake...

953
01:04:32.480 --> 01:04:33.560
Okay. your wheel.

954
01:04:36.120 --> 01:04:37.680
- Straight?
- Right...

955
01:04:37.760 --> 01:04:38.760
Got it.

956
01:04:47.120 --> 01:04:48.800
- Which way now?
- Left...

957
01:04:56.920 --> 01:04:58.440
Okay. You're good...

958
01:05:03.400 --> 01:05:04.400
That's a person.

959
01:05:06.920 --> 01:05:08.400
- Okay. Car...
- I see it.

960
01:05:34.320 --> 01:05:35.320
Hit it.

961
01:05:42.320 --> 01:05:43.320
Hang on!

962
01:05:44.200 --> 01:05:45.200
Go...!

963
01:05:54.800 --> 01:05:56.440
What is happening?
Where are we going?

964
01:05:56.520 --> 01:05:57.520
I don't know.

965
01:05:58.600 --> 01:05:59.920
Okay. brake...!

966
01:06:28.480 --> 01:06:29.600
Don't hate me.

967
01:06:32.920 --> 01:06:34.520
Grace? Grace!

968
01:06:49.280 --> 01:06:50.320
Come on. come on. come on.

969
01:07:17.520 --> 01:07:18.520
Ethan!

970
01:07:19.120 --> 01:07:20.120
Ethan!

971
01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:25.600
Well. come on.

972
01:08:18.400 --> 01:08:20.720
All right. We know
Grace has one half of the key.

973
01:08:20.800 --> 01:08:23.360
We also know she's gonna be
at the Ducale at midnight.

974
01:08:23.440 --> 01:08:24.840
And now we have a pretty good idea

975
01:08:24.920 --> 01:08:26.920
as to who is gonna
be waiting for her there.

976
01:08:27.000 --> 01:08:28.000
The event is being hosted

977
01:08:28.080 --> 01:08:30.456
by none other than our favorite
international arms trafficker

978
01:08:30.480 --> 01:08:32.680
and black marketeer.
Alana Mitsopolis.

979
01:08:32.880 --> 01:08:34.480
The White Widow.

980
01:08:34.960 --> 01:08:37.400
Does she know who you actually are
or does she still think

981
01:08:37.480 --> 01:08:40.160
you're the globally notorious
mass murderer John Lark?

982
01:08:40.240 --> 01:08:41.240
Who says I'm not?

983
01:08:42.280 --> 01:08:44.200
Didn't she put a price
on your head in Paris?

984
01:08:44.280 --> 01:08:48.400
She did indeed.
She and Ethan. they worked it out.

985
01:08:48.840 --> 01:08:50.160
You never did tell me how.

986
01:08:50.560 --> 01:08:52.200
Can we continue. please?

987
01:08:52.640 --> 01:08:55.920
Right. So. assuming we get
the complete key at the party tonight

988
01:08:56.000 --> 01:08:59.000
we still don't know what it unlocks.
so we need to find somebody who does.

989
01:08:59.080 --> 01:09:01.680
The question is
where to start looking.

990
01:09:01.760 --> 01:09:04.720
We figured that the bomb didn't
just walk into the airport by itself.

991
01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:05.960
Right? Somebody put it there.

992
01:09:06.200 --> 01:09:08.320
Somebody working for the Entity.

993
01:09:08.560 --> 01:09:11.720
This is everything I captured from
the security cameras at the airport

994
01:09:11.800 --> 01:09:14.080
up to the minute
everything went haywire.

995
01:09:14.240 --> 01:09:17.160
And this is the feed
from your AR sunglasses.

996
01:09:17.240 --> 01:09:20.200
I've been running facial recognition
on everyone in the airport.

997
01:09:20.280 --> 01:09:21.480
See anything strange?

998
01:09:24.760 --> 01:09:25.920
It's like a ghost.

999
01:09:26.440 --> 01:09:27.880
Ghosts don't have reflections.

1000
01:09:31.360 --> 01:09:34.680
The only person in the airport
with no identity.

1001
01:09:35.280 --> 01:09:39.320
The only man who can't be found
anyplace else in the airport

1002
01:09:39.640 --> 01:09:41.920
except that reflection.

1003
01:09:42.680 --> 01:09:44.200
He's being erased.

1004
01:09:44.720 --> 01:09:46.200
In real time.

1005
01:09:52.680 --> 01:09:53.920
The Entity.

1006
01:09:55.160 --> 01:09:56.440
It's protecting him.

1007
01:09:57.000 --> 01:09:58.920
You saw him. didn't you?

1008
01:10:01.280 --> 01:10:02.600
I wasn't sure.

1009
01:10:04.200 --> 01:10:05.240
Well. who is he?

1010
01:10:12.400 --> 01:10:14.120
Someone I thought

1011
01:10:15.320 --> 01:10:16.920
died a long time ago.

1012
01:10:17.240 --> 01:10:18.600
In another life.

1013
01:10:19.160 --> 01:10:20.600
Before the IMF.

1014
01:10:21.680 --> 01:10:24.480
Before I was offered the choice.

1015
01:10:27.480 --> 01:10:29.000
And in a very real sense

1016
01:10:29.840 --> 01:10:32.000
he made me who I am today.

1017
01:10:33.560 --> 01:10:34.720
Does he have a name?

1018
01:10:35.520 --> 01:10:37.680
He calls himself Gabriel.

1019
01:10:40.600 --> 01:10:41.920
You know him.

1020
01:10:44.080 --> 01:10:45.880
There is no knowing him.

1021
01:10:47.000 --> 01:10:49.240
He has no recorded past.

1022
01:10:49.320 --> 01:10:51.240
The Entity made sure of that.

1023
01:10:52.200 --> 01:10:53.480
He's a dark messiah.

1024
01:10:53.800 --> 01:10:56.040
The Entity's chosen messenger.

1025
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:58.000
And he sees death

1026
01:10:59.080 --> 01:11:02.600
as a gift he wants to share
with the rest of the world.

1027
01:11:03.240 --> 01:11:04.240
How do you know this?

1028
01:11:04.480 --> 01:11:07.200
I still have
a few friends left in MI6.

1029
01:11:07.920 --> 01:11:09.320
Friends who are afraid

1030
01:11:09.400 --> 01:11:12.320
of the British government
gaining control of the Entity.

1031
01:11:12.960 --> 01:11:16.240
Any attempt to try to stop them
would be seen as an act of treason.

1032
01:11:16.320 --> 01:11:17.800
And because you're disavowed

1033
01:11:17.880 --> 01:11:21.480
your friends called
and asked you for help.

1034
01:11:21.560 --> 01:11:23.640
They knew Gabriel serves the Entity.

1035
01:11:24.280 --> 01:11:26.040
They knew he was
on his way to Istanbul

1036
01:11:26.120 --> 01:11:29.920
to acquire one half
of a cruciform key.

1037
01:11:30.720 --> 01:11:33.520
So I beat him to it.

1038
01:11:34.840 --> 01:11:36.920
And when Kittridge put
a bounty on your head

1039
01:11:37.920 --> 01:11:39.760
you went to the desert to hide.

1040
01:11:40.200 --> 01:11:42.560
But somehow the bounty hunters
found you anyway.

1041
01:11:42.640 --> 01:11:43.640
Yes.

1042
01:11:43.720 --> 01:11:47.880
So. did these friends of yours
happen to say what the key unlocks?

1043
01:11:47.960 --> 01:11:51.600
MI6 suspects it leads somehow
to the Entity's source code.

1044
01:11:52.280 --> 01:11:53.400
Source code.

1045
01:11:54.560 --> 01:11:55.880
When were you gonna tell me this?

1046
01:11:57.000 --> 01:11:58.040
I'm telling you now.

1047
01:11:59.720 --> 01:12:02.040
Your friends at MI6.
how'd they contact you?

1048
01:12:02.120 --> 01:12:03.920
Did you speak with them?
Face to face?

1049
01:12:04.000 --> 01:12:05.160
I'm disavowed.

1050
01:12:05.440 --> 01:12:09.320
They couldn't risk meeting me
in person. so all communication...

1051
01:12:11.520 --> 01:12:14.400
Electronic. Was digital.

1052
01:12:17.720 --> 01:12:19.560
No. We can't be sure
that was the Entity.

1053
01:12:19.880 --> 01:12:21.480
We can't be sure it wasn't.

1054
01:12:21.560 --> 01:12:24.800
No. we can't be sure anything is real
outside of this very conversation.

1055
01:12:26.480 --> 01:12:27.560
None of you should be here.

1056
01:12:27.720 --> 01:12:30.000
- Ethan...
- No. You don't know Gabriel. I do.

1057
01:12:30.280 --> 01:12:31.800
It's not the killing he enjoys.

1058
01:12:31.880 --> 01:12:33.720
It's the suffering it causes.

1059
01:12:33.800 --> 01:12:35.720
And he knows
the best way to get to me

1060
01:12:36.400 --> 01:12:37.880
is through all of you.

1061
01:12:39.040 --> 01:12:40.680
And if Gabriel knows me...

1062
01:12:41.080 --> 01:12:42.320
The Entity knows.

1063
01:12:42.760 --> 01:12:44.760
There's a reason
he wants me here. There's...

1064
01:12:45.760 --> 01:12:47.160
There's a reason he wants you here.

1065
01:12:47.240 --> 01:12:48.800
It wants you here.

1066
01:12:48.880 --> 01:12:52.320
"Who or what is
the most important thing to you?"

1067
01:12:53.360 --> 01:12:55.280
No. You have to go.
You all... you have to go.

1068
01:12:55.360 --> 01:12:57.000
Ethan. what if it wants us to leave?

1069
01:12:57.080 --> 01:12:58.376
Like you made us leave the airport.

1070
01:12:58.400 --> 01:13:00.600
And what if it wants you alone
at that party tonight?

1071
01:13:00.680 --> 01:13:02.896
Then I go alone. At least I don't
have all of you to worry about.

1072
01:13:02.920 --> 01:13:04.960
This is exactly why
I didn't want to tell you.

1073
01:13:05.040 --> 01:13:07.320
Ethan. you're playing
four-dimensional chess

1074
01:13:07.400 --> 01:13:08.520
with an algorithm.

1075
01:13:08.600 --> 01:13:10.200
The Entity knows who we are.

1076
01:13:10.360 --> 01:13:12.280
Any move we make.
it's probably considered it.

1077
01:13:12.360 --> 01:13:15.600
Anything we do. we have to assume
that it's counting on us to do it.

1078
01:13:15.680 --> 01:13:19.480
If you want to beat this thing.
you have to start thinking like it.

1079
01:13:19.560 --> 01:13:22.800
Cold. logical. unemotional.

1080
01:13:23.080 --> 01:13:26.200
If that key really does
grant control of the Entity

1081
01:13:26.560 --> 01:13:29.520
Gabriel is the last person on Earth
who should have it.

1082
01:13:29.600 --> 01:13:31.120
She's right. Ethan.

1083
01:13:31.440 --> 01:13:33.560
Gabriel cannot have that key.

1084
01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:37.920
And none of our lives
can matter more than this mission.

1085
01:13:44.240 --> 01:13:45.760
I don't accept that.

1086
01:14:11.160 --> 01:14:13.000
It's my first time in Venice.

1087
01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:18.200
It's mine. too.

1088
01:15:17.400 --> 01:15:18.440
Buy you a drink?

1089
01:15:19.520 --> 01:15:20.760
I'm waiting for someone.

1090
01:15:21.280 --> 01:15:22.280
So am I.

1091
01:15:24.360 --> 01:15:27.120
We can wait together. I'm Gabriel.

1092
01:15:27.440 --> 01:15:28.440
If you say so.

1093
01:15:29.480 --> 01:15:30.640
And you're Grace.

1094
01:15:40.120 --> 01:15:41.200
I don't have it on me.

1095
01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:42.800
I wouldn't expect you to.

1096
01:15:43.680 --> 01:15:45.360
In any case.
I'm not here for the key.

1097
01:15:46.600 --> 01:15:49.040
- What do you want?
- Suppose while we're waiting

1098
01:15:49.120 --> 01:15:50.200
I tell you a little story.

1099
01:15:50.440 --> 01:15:52.456
You're obviously not the person
I came here to meet.

1100
01:15:52.480 --> 01:15:54.160
It's your story. Grace.

1101
01:15:55.400 --> 01:15:56.880
I know how it ends.

1102
01:15:58.440 --> 01:16:00.600
Let me buy you a drink
and perhaps we can change it.

1103
01:16:27.520 --> 01:16:28.680
Let's go to a party.

1104
01:16:36.680 --> 01:16:37.680
Excuse me. sir.

1105
01:16:39.800 --> 01:16:41.000
Would you please follow me?

1106
01:16:43.000 --> 01:16:46.600
It's important you understand
that you're not unique.

1107
01:16:47.360 --> 01:16:48.360
30 years ago...

1108
01:16:49.320 --> 01:16:50.520
her name was Marie.

1109
01:16:51.040 --> 01:16:54.080
The first of many women
who trusted our mutual friend.

1110
01:16:54.160 --> 01:16:56.320
Women who all have
something he wants.

1111
01:16:57.120 --> 01:17:00.800
Women who are all in over
their heads. or so he tells them.

1112
01:17:01.360 --> 01:17:02.680
Sound familiar?

1113
01:17:03.160 --> 01:17:04.680
What happened to Marie?

1114
01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:07.320
Same thing that happens
to all the women he uses

1115
01:17:08.520 --> 01:17:11.080
as well as anyone else
who touches that key.

1116
01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:13.400
He doesn't care
whether people live or die.

1117
01:17:13.480 --> 01:17:16.720
He cares only about his objective.

1118
01:17:17.720 --> 01:17:19.640
And right now.
the only thing standing in his way

1119
01:17:20.280 --> 01:17:21.280
is you.

1120
01:17:22.400 --> 01:17:23.640
Why should I believe you?

1121
01:17:23.720 --> 01:17:24.720
You shouldn't.

1122
01:17:24.800 --> 01:17:27.000
You've stepped
into a world of lies. Grace.

1123
01:17:27.360 --> 01:17:29.120
Nothing anyone says is true.

1124
01:17:29.400 --> 01:17:32.400
Just remember that
when he promises to protect you.

1125
01:17:32.640 --> 01:17:33.640
Grace.

1126
01:17:47.360 --> 01:17:49.040
It's been a long time. Ethan.

1127
01:17:50.120 --> 01:17:52.080
You should've killed me
when you had the chance.

1128
01:17:53.200 --> 01:17:55.400
Good evening. everyone.

1129
01:17:55.960 --> 01:17:58.320
If it isn't John Lark.

1130
01:17:59.400 --> 01:18:01.440
Except it isn't. actually.

1131
01:18:02.040 --> 01:18:06.560
But until you're ready to tell me
your real name. Lark will have to do.

1132
01:18:07.480 --> 01:18:09.040
It's good to see you. Alana.

1133
01:18:12.600 --> 01:18:15.200
And you're Gabriel. I presume.

1134
01:18:15.760 --> 01:18:18.200
I've heard so very little about you.

1135
01:18:18.880 --> 01:18:21.840
Aren't you so much
more handsome in person?

1136
01:18:24.320 --> 01:18:26.600
Such a gentleman. too.

1137
01:18:31.320 --> 01:18:32.920
And you must be Grace.

1138
01:18:35.920 --> 01:18:38.000
Should I know you?

1139
01:18:38.320 --> 01:18:40.800
I believe you have something for me.

1140
01:18:41.200 --> 01:18:42.640
You hired me.

1141
01:18:43.040 --> 01:18:44.800
Oh. I handpicked you.

1142
01:18:54.600 --> 01:18:55.600
Don't!

1143
01:18:57.480 --> 01:18:58.480
You don't.

1144
01:19:18.920 --> 01:19:19.960
She doesn't have it.

1145
01:19:21.200 --> 01:19:22.280
Where is it?

1146
01:19:22.360 --> 01:19:24.800
It's in the last place
you would ever think to look.

1147
01:19:27.800 --> 01:19:29.680
Why don't we go upstairs
and have a drink?

1148
01:19:48.120 --> 01:19:49.160
Damn.

1149
01:19:49.240 --> 01:19:52.200
As most of you know.
I am merely a broker.

1150
01:19:52.600 --> 01:19:54.200
I connect a buyer and a seller.

1151
01:19:54.280 --> 01:19:56.880
Sometimes for money.
sometimes for information

1152
01:19:56.960 --> 01:19:59.800
but mostly for friendship.

1153
01:20:00.600 --> 01:20:03.280
I just want everyone to get along.

1154
01:20:04.200 --> 01:20:06.400
With me. especially.

1155
01:20:06.680 --> 01:20:09.520
But the world is changing.

1156
01:20:09.640 --> 01:20:11.360
Truth is vanishing.

1157
01:20:11.680 --> 01:20:13.480
War is coming.

1158
01:20:13.560 --> 01:20:18.200
And the key to world domination
is. of all things. a key.

1159
01:20:18.800 --> 01:20:21.720
One with the power
to control the Entity.

1160
01:20:22.320 --> 01:20:23.960
One that any government in the world

1161
01:20:24.040 --> 01:20:27.000
would pay a king's ransom
to take possession of.

1162
01:20:27.600 --> 01:20:29.160
And some of my dearest friends

1163
01:20:29.240 --> 01:20:31.360
in this case.
every major nuclear power

1164
01:20:31.440 --> 01:20:32.680
and a handful of minor ones

1165
01:20:32.760 --> 01:20:34.600
have asked me to deliver this key.

1166
01:20:34.680 --> 01:20:37.320
Of course. if you do find the key

1167
01:20:37.400 --> 01:20:39.520
you'll be forced to confront
an impossible dilemma.

1168
01:20:39.600 --> 01:20:42.600
Whoever you give the key to
will be forever in your debt.

1169
01:20:42.680 --> 01:20:45.960
But to the rest of the world.
you'll be an enemy.

1170
01:20:46.520 --> 01:20:47.800
Oh. I like her.

1171
01:20:48.080 --> 01:20:50.480
What's your relationship with him?

1172
01:20:50.560 --> 01:20:53.160
Gabriel represents
another interested party.

1173
01:20:53.720 --> 01:20:56.240
In fact. this party

1174
01:20:56.320 --> 01:20:59.760
was arranged
by that interested party.

1175
01:20:59.840 --> 01:21:03.800
You could even say that
this party is that interested party.

1176
01:21:36.160 --> 01:21:37.200
Is this...

1177
01:21:38.200 --> 01:21:39.400
The Entity.

1178
01:21:41.440 --> 01:21:43.520
And so the plot thickens.

1179
01:21:44.280 --> 01:21:46.480
Do I give the key
to one of my old friends

1180
01:21:46.560 --> 01:21:49.920
or do I hand it and my fate
over to Gabriel

1181
01:21:50.000 --> 01:21:52.840
and his infernal machine?

1182
01:21:54.280 --> 01:21:57.400
What makes you so sure
you'll get the completed key?

1183
01:21:59.000 --> 01:22:00.280
You have one half of it.

1184
01:22:00.720 --> 01:22:04.400
And she knows
where the other half is.

1185
01:22:06.960 --> 01:22:09.200
Assuming you can get it

1186
01:22:10.160 --> 01:22:13.480
why don't you just keep the key
and all that power for yourself?

1187
01:22:13.560 --> 01:22:15.800
Because she doesn't know
what it unlocks

1188
01:22:16.240 --> 01:22:18.080
any more than the rest of us.

1189
01:22:19.080 --> 01:22:21.240
So. like it or not.
you have to choose a suitor.

1190
01:22:21.320 --> 01:22:25.120
It's distastefully put. Lark.
but it's true.

1191
01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:27.880
Of course I know what it unlocks.

1192
01:22:29.080 --> 01:22:31.360
And what's he offering for the key?

1193
01:22:31.440 --> 01:22:34.720
As I've explained to Grace before.
I'm not here for any key

1194
01:22:35.040 --> 01:22:37.200
as I'll have both halves
in hand tomorrow.

1195
01:22:37.840 --> 01:22:39.520
What makes you so certain of that?

1196
01:22:39.600 --> 01:22:42.240
You've no idea
of the power I represent.

1197
01:22:42.320 --> 01:22:45.720
Thousands of quadrillions
of computations per millisecond

1198
01:22:45.960 --> 01:22:49.120
subtly manipulating
the minds of billions

1199
01:22:49.200 --> 01:22:51.960
while parsing
every possible cause and effect

1200
01:22:52.040 --> 01:22:54.560
every scenario. however implausible

1201
01:22:54.640 --> 01:22:58.600
into a very real map
of a most probable next.

1202
01:22:58.960 --> 01:23:01.520
And with only a few changes
to the present

1203
01:23:02.120 --> 01:23:04.760
the future is all but assured.

1204
01:23:05.760 --> 01:23:07.600
The key will come to me.

1205
01:23:08.360 --> 01:23:09.360
Tomorrow.

1206
01:23:10.240 --> 01:23:13.000
On the Orient Express
bound for Innsbruck.

1207
01:23:13.080 --> 01:23:14.080
Innsbruck?

1208
01:23:14.520 --> 01:23:15.800
It knows.

1209
01:23:16.200 --> 01:23:18.880
It knows that
you've already chosen your suitor.

1210
01:23:19.200 --> 01:23:22.120
It knows that you intend to mate
the two halves of the key

1211
01:23:22.200 --> 01:23:23.920
in a desperate grasp for control.

1212
01:23:24.720 --> 01:23:27.440
I. however. have been promised
the completed key

1213
01:23:27.720 --> 01:23:29.360
will lay itself at my feet

1214
01:23:30.120 --> 01:23:32.920
provided someone dies tonight.

1215
01:23:34.280 --> 01:23:35.320
Who?

1216
01:23:36.200 --> 01:23:37.200
Her.

1217
01:23:38.840 --> 01:23:40.320
Or her.

1218
01:23:42.240 --> 01:23:44.200
And you will bear witness. Ethan.

1219
01:23:44.560 --> 01:23:48.240
The key will be mine.
and I will be gone

1220
01:23:48.320 --> 01:23:50.440
like smoke in a hurricane.

1221
01:23:50.720 --> 01:23:53.480
But only after
someone you care about dies.

1222
01:23:55.800 --> 01:23:56.840
It is written.

1223
01:23:58.480 --> 01:23:59.480
You see what this is

1224
01:24:00.680 --> 01:24:01.680
don't you?

1225
01:24:03.280 --> 01:24:04.640
He's afraid.

1226
01:24:05.600 --> 01:24:06.720
It's afraid.

1227
01:24:07.880 --> 01:24:09.880
Somehow it knows we're close.

1228
01:24:10.840 --> 01:24:12.120
Why else would you be here?

1229
01:24:13.000 --> 01:24:16.560
Help me. Help me complete the key.
and I will kill this thing.

1230
01:24:16.760 --> 01:24:18.400
It knows your every secret. Alana.

1231
01:24:18.480 --> 01:24:20.200
Don't listen to this fanatic.

1232
01:24:20.280 --> 01:24:21.680
Help him and you'll die. too.

1233
01:24:21.760 --> 01:24:23.760
Help him. everyone dies.

1234
01:24:23.840 --> 01:24:25.120
I'll see you tomorrow.

1235
01:24:27.080 --> 01:24:28.080
Alana?

1236
01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:37.120
His fate is written.

1237
01:24:37.760 --> 01:24:39.160
Shall we write yours. too?

1238
01:24:40.760 --> 01:24:41.760
Alana.

1239
01:24:44.800 --> 01:24:47.240
I'm sorry. Lark.

1240
01:24:57.760 --> 01:25:00.360
For old times' sake.
I'll let you choose which one.

1241
01:25:01.760 --> 01:25:02.760
Ilsa...

1242
01:25:03.200 --> 01:25:04.320
or Grace.

1243
01:25:04.720 --> 01:25:06.480
Kill him. Zola. Kill him.

1244
01:25:06.600 --> 01:25:07.640
Kill him where he stands!

1245
01:25:07.720 --> 01:25:09.400
The choice is yours then. Alana.

1246
01:25:09.480 --> 01:25:10.560
Though I'll remind you

1247
01:25:10.640 --> 01:25:12.800
Grace knows where half the key is.

1248
01:25:13.920 --> 01:25:16.560
If anything happens to either of them

1249
01:25:16.880 --> 01:25:20.600
there is no place on Earth where
you or your god will be safe from me.

1250
01:25:20.960 --> 01:25:24.680
There's no place that I won't go
to kill you. That is written.

1251
01:25:24.760 --> 01:25:26.080
It's good to see you. old friend.

1252
01:25:57.840 --> 01:26:00.840
You have made a terrible mistake.

1253
01:26:00.920 --> 01:26:03.040
My life is on the line here.

1254
01:26:03.520 --> 01:26:05.560
I have to be on that train tomorrow.

1255
01:26:06.880 --> 01:26:09.040
And I have to have that key.

1256
01:26:10.600 --> 01:26:13.360
And I do not care how I get it.

1257
01:26:17.480 --> 01:26:18.480
Don't move.

1258
01:26:24.000 --> 01:26:25.040
Run as far as you can.

1259
01:27:03.800 --> 01:27:04.800
What the f...

1260
01:28:06.200 --> 01:28:07.440
Grace...!

1261
01:28:08.600 --> 01:28:09.600
Grace!

1262
01:28:24.040 --> 01:28:26.280
<i>Luther. Benji.
if you hear me. I need eyes.</i>

1263
01:28:26.360 --> 01:28:28.600
<i>Grace is leaving the Ducale on foot.
She has the key.</i>

1264
01:28:28.680 --> 01:28:30.720
- We're here. Go.
<i>- Need to find her. Where is she?</i>

1265
01:28:31.600 --> 01:28:33.720
Damn it! I've lost picture.
I need another satellite.

1266
01:28:33.960 --> 01:28:35.920
Hacking the Russian Zenith Four
spy satellite.

1267
01:28:36.000 --> 01:28:37.880
We're scraping the barrel.
but it'll have to do.

1268
01:28:46.120 --> 01:28:47.120
This way!

1269
01:29:05.720 --> 01:29:06.720
Where am I going?

1270
01:29:07.040 --> 01:29:08.160
Where am I going? Come on...

1271
01:29:08.200 --> 01:29:10.080
- <i>Stand by...</i>
- Just hurry. Hurry. hurry.

1272
01:29:10.160 --> 01:29:11.736
She's just north of you.
crossing the bridge.

1273
01:29:11.760 --> 01:29:12.816
<i>Say again. Benji. Say again.</i>

1274
01:29:12.840 --> 01:29:14.800
Just head north. Ethan.
She's crossing the bridge.

1275
01:29:31.800 --> 01:29:33.600
<i>Ethan. take the passage
to your right.</i>

1276
01:29:33.680 --> 01:29:35.256
- Yeah. I see it!
- <i>Down that narrow alley</i>

1277
01:29:35.280 --> 01:29:36.360
<i>and turn left.</i>

1278
01:29:37.080 --> 01:29:39.040
- I'm losing picture again.
- Looking for another.

1279
01:29:39.400 --> 01:29:42.600
The Entity is knocking out satellites
faster than I can hack into them.

1280
01:30:07.040 --> 01:30:08.040
<i>Benji. I don't see her.</i>

1281
01:30:08.120 --> 01:30:09.496
<i>- Where is she?
- Down the narrow alley</i>

1282
01:30:09.520 --> 01:30:10.920
<i>- and turn left.
- Okay. copy that.</i>

1283
01:30:12.360 --> 01:30:13.360
<i>Turn right.</i>

1284
01:30:13.440 --> 01:30:15.680
<i>Sorry. my mistake.
I meant left. Another left.</i>

1285
01:30:15.760 --> 01:30:16.760
Oh. my God.

1286
01:30:17.200 --> 01:30:19.800
Ethan. our comms have been breached!
You're talking to the Entity!

1287
01:30:20.240 --> 01:30:23.280
<i>Turn left. Turn right.
Take the bridge to your left.</i>

1288
01:30:23.360 --> 01:30:25.200
Ethan. that is not me! Do you copy?

1289
01:30:25.280 --> 01:30:26.320
Ethan. come in.

1290
01:30:26.440 --> 01:30:28.520
<i>Down the alley to your left.
Turn left.</i>

1291
01:30:29.040 --> 01:30:30.040
<i>Turn right.</i>

1292
01:30:32.040 --> 01:30:33.160
Try to reestablish comms.

1293
01:30:33.240 --> 01:30:35.096
- Wait. where are you going?
- I'm gonna try and find Ethan.

1294
01:30:35.120 --> 01:30:36.920
<i>Go to the end of the alley
and turn right.</i>

1295
01:30:37.200 --> 01:30:40.680
<i>Ethan. I see Grace about 800 meters
in front of you. Take that passage.</i>

1296
01:30:49.800 --> 01:30:51.600
- <i>Wait...! Not that way!</i>
- What. why?

1297
01:30:52.200 --> 01:30:53.280
Which way...?

1298
01:30:54.000 --> 01:30:55.160
Wait. Left or right?

1299
01:30:55.240 --> 01:30:56.280
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

1300
01:30:57.680 --> 01:30:59.336
What do you mean. it doesn't matter?
Where is she?

1301
01:30:59.360 --> 01:31:01.400
<i>She's on her way to the Minich Bridge</i>

1302
01:31:03.200 --> 01:31:05.200
<i>where Gabriel is waiting.</i>

1303
01:31:05.880 --> 01:31:07.600
<i>You will never get there in time.</i>

1304
01:31:08.800 --> 01:31:10.520
<i>But you can. Ilsa.</i>

1305
01:31:11.800 --> 01:31:14.200
<i>I know what matters most
to you. Ethan.</i>

1306
01:31:14.760 --> 01:31:16.080
This isn't Benji.

1307
01:31:16.160 --> 01:31:17.640
<i>No. it's not.</i>

1308
01:31:18.440 --> 01:31:20.120
<i>But you are done.</i>

1309
01:31:42.680 --> 01:31:43.760
So be it.

1310
01:34:13.680 --> 01:34:15.520
I was hoping it'd be you.

1311
01:37:37.200 --> 01:37:38.560
I'm sorry.

1312
01:37:39.680 --> 01:37:41.320
I've forgotten your name.

1313
01:37:41.400 --> 01:37:42.400
Luther.

1314
01:37:44.160 --> 01:37:45.160
Benji.

1315
01:37:46.800 --> 01:37:47.800
And her?

1316
01:37:48.840 --> 01:37:49.960
Ilsa.

1317
01:37:51.600 --> 01:37:52.920
Were you close?

1318
01:37:53.880 --> 01:37:55.000
You and she?

1319
01:37:55.680 --> 01:37:56.960
In our way.

1320
01:37:59.560 --> 01:38:00.920
I'm the reason she's dead.

1321
01:38:01.000 --> 01:38:02.000
No.

1322
01:38:02.080 --> 01:38:04.000
She's the reason you're alive.

1323
01:38:04.480 --> 01:38:05.880
And that's the truth.

1324
01:38:06.320 --> 01:38:07.920
I don't know how to feel about it.

1325
01:38:08.320 --> 01:38:09.840
You probably never will.

1326
01:38:11.680 --> 01:38:13.000
I'm so sorry.

1327
01:38:14.600 --> 01:38:16.560
If there's anything
I can do to help...

1328
01:38:17.120 --> 01:38:18.800
That's what we'd like
to talk to you about.

1329
01:38:20.880 --> 01:38:23.000
In a little over three hours

1330
01:38:23.360 --> 01:38:27.760
the White Widow is expected to be
on the Orient Express to Innsbruck

1331
01:38:27.840 --> 01:38:28.960
where a buyer is waiting

1332
01:38:29.040 --> 01:38:31.760
to take receipt of
the complete and verified key.

1333
01:38:31.840 --> 01:38:33.840
But she doesn't have
the complete key.

1334
01:38:33.920 --> 01:38:35.040
That Widow doesn't.

1335
01:38:37.440 --> 01:38:38.720
But ours could.

1336
01:38:39.000 --> 01:38:41.120
What is that?

1337
01:38:41.960 --> 01:38:43.880
Your chance to be someone else.

1338
01:38:44.000 --> 01:38:45.000
I don't understand.

1339
01:38:45.080 --> 01:38:46.760
We're not gonna lie to you. Grace.

1340
01:38:46.840 --> 01:38:47.896
You're in a lot of trouble.

1341
01:38:47.920 --> 01:38:50.480
No number of fake passports
is gonna get you out of this one.

1342
01:38:50.560 --> 01:38:52.000
Governments know who you are.

1343
01:38:52.080 --> 01:38:53.400
The White Widow knows.

1344
01:38:53.600 --> 01:38:54.880
And the Entity knows.

1345
01:38:55.160 --> 01:38:58.120
Your future boils down
to three options now.

1346
01:38:58.200 --> 01:38:59.200
Prison.

1347
01:38:59.440 --> 01:39:00.440
Death.

1348
01:39:00.520 --> 01:39:01.680
Or the choice.

1349
01:39:02.200 --> 01:39:03.360
The choice?

1350
01:39:03.880 --> 01:39:08.120
At one time or another. each of us
was in a similar situation to yours.

1351
01:39:08.200 --> 01:39:10.640
And each of us
was offered the choice.

1352
01:39:10.960 --> 01:39:12.600
The same choice
we're offering you now.

1353
01:39:13.000 --> 01:39:14.000
Which is?

1354
01:39:14.920 --> 01:39:16.280
To come with us.

1355
01:39:17.600 --> 01:39:19.000
And be a ghost.

1356
01:40:50.800 --> 01:40:52.800
Wait.... Stop...

1357
01:40:53.840 --> 01:40:55.040
You're not serious.

1358
01:40:55.120 --> 01:40:57.720
Well. you did say
you'd do anything to help.

1359
01:40:57.800 --> 01:41:01.480
And you jump off the train
with the key?

1360
01:41:01.720 --> 01:41:02.720
Yes.

1361
01:41:02.800 --> 01:41:03.800
You.

1362
01:41:04.160 --> 01:41:06.200
- Not us.
- Yes.

1363
01:41:07.040 --> 01:41:08.040
And what happens to me?

1364
01:41:08.120 --> 01:41:11.240
You'll be taken into custody
by Clandestine Services

1365
01:41:11.320 --> 01:41:14.600
most likely the same men that
have been chasing me since Abu Dhabi.

1366
01:41:15.200 --> 01:41:17.600
Shortly thereafter.
a man will come to see you.

1367
01:41:17.680 --> 01:41:19.520
His name is Eugene Kittridge.

1368
01:41:19.920 --> 01:41:22.560
You'll tell him I sent you.
that I gave you the choice

1369
01:41:23.320 --> 01:41:25.200
and that you choose to accept.

1370
01:41:27.080 --> 01:41:29.760
And you trust this Kittridge person?

1371
01:41:30.600 --> 01:41:32.560
I trust him to recognize your value.

1372
01:41:34.160 --> 01:41:35.240
He'll want to use you.

1373
01:41:36.200 --> 01:41:38.720
And after that. it's what?

1374
01:41:39.320 --> 01:41:40.320
This?

1375
01:41:41.480 --> 01:41:42.680
When do I get my life back?

1376
01:41:42.880 --> 01:41:43.880
What life?

1377
01:41:44.800 --> 01:41:45.880
I mean it. Grace.

1378
01:41:46.080 --> 01:41:47.080
What life?

1379
01:41:47.280 --> 01:41:49.200
I lived that life.

1380
01:41:49.600 --> 01:41:50.640
We all did.

1381
01:41:50.720 --> 01:41:53.000
Nobody's making us do this. Grace.

1382
01:41:53.520 --> 01:41:55.040
We're here because we want to be.

1383
01:41:56.200 --> 01:41:57.800
I tell you what.
I'll give you a one-off.

1384
01:41:58.040 --> 01:41:59.696
I'll help you find the key
and your friends

1385
01:41:59.720 --> 01:42:00.760
wipe my slate clean.

1386
01:42:00.840 --> 01:42:02.760
New name.
little bit of walking-around money...

1387
01:42:02.840 --> 01:42:03.840
You'll be dead.

1388
01:42:04.160 --> 01:42:08.560
Without a team. your life won't be
measured in years or even months.

1389
01:42:08.800 --> 01:42:10.680
It'll be measured in hours.

1390
01:42:11.040 --> 01:42:14.040
But if I stay. I'll be safe.

1391
01:42:14.920 --> 01:42:16.640
You'll protect me. is that it?

1392
01:42:16.720 --> 01:42:17.920
- Yes.
- No.

1393
01:42:20.480 --> 01:42:22.200
I can't promise you that.

1394
01:42:23.360 --> 01:42:24.560
None of us can.

1395
01:42:27.200 --> 01:42:28.400
But I swear

1396
01:42:29.720 --> 01:42:30.960
your life

1397
01:42:31.720 --> 01:42:34.520
will always matter more to me
than my own.

1398
01:42:42.480 --> 01:42:43.880
You don't even know me.

1399
01:42:46.480 --> 01:42:48.200
What difference does that make?

1400
01:43:07.000 --> 01:43:10.120
I packed you a BASE parachute
and a speed wing

1401
01:43:10.200 --> 01:43:12.120
depending on how
you need to leave the train.

1402
01:43:12.200 --> 01:43:15.360
And I modified our comms
to use sky wave radio.

1403
01:43:15.440 --> 01:43:17.120
Not as reliable as satellite

1404
01:43:17.200 --> 01:43:20.320
but completely analog.
immune to the Entity.

1405
01:43:20.400 --> 01:43:21.400
I got it.

1406
01:43:22.680 --> 01:43:23.880
This is where I leave you.

1407
01:43:27.600 --> 01:43:30.440
This is the drive from the laptop
I was using last night.

1408
01:43:30.760 --> 01:43:34.040
If there's even a trace
of the Entity's encoding in there

1409
01:43:34.120 --> 01:43:35.200
I'll find it.

1410
01:43:35.560 --> 01:43:37.880
But it's going to take
everything I've got.

1411
01:43:37.960 --> 01:43:40.200
I have to work
completely offline in a place

1412
01:43:40.280 --> 01:43:42.040
where the Entity can't find me.

1413
01:43:42.640 --> 01:43:43.880
I have to go.

1414
01:43:45.080 --> 01:43:46.160
I understand.

1415
01:43:47.520 --> 01:43:48.520
Now...

1416
01:43:51.120 --> 01:43:53.120
I have to ask you a question.

1417
01:43:54.120 --> 01:43:56.720
Not as your partner.
but as your friend.

1418
01:43:58.080 --> 01:43:59.240
What's your objective?

1419
01:44:00.480 --> 01:44:01.680
Kill the Entity.

1420
01:44:02.080 --> 01:44:04.400
What about killing Gabriel?

1421
01:44:06.720 --> 01:44:08.520
He knows what the key unlocks.

1422
01:44:09.520 --> 01:44:10.960
We need him alive.

1423
01:44:11.040 --> 01:44:12.600
I haven't forgotten that.

1424
01:44:13.240 --> 01:44:17.520
Will you still remember that
when you're looking him in the eye?

1425
01:44:19.360 --> 01:44:20.360
Think about it.

1426
01:44:20.640 --> 01:44:25.520
Why else would the Entity want him
to kill someone you care about?

1427
01:44:26.280 --> 01:44:29.400
Everyone else thinks
they can control the Entity.

1428
01:44:29.840 --> 01:44:32.000
Only you want to kill it.

1429
01:44:32.840 --> 01:44:35.120
In some probable future

1430
01:44:35.560 --> 01:44:37.240
it sees you winning. Ethan.

1431
01:44:37.720 --> 01:44:39.120
And it's afraid.

1432
01:44:39.840 --> 01:44:42.800
It's afraid
of you taking Gabriel alive

1433
01:44:42.880 --> 01:44:45.760
and forcing him to tell you
what the key unlocks.

1434
01:44:47.120 --> 01:44:50.680
I believe it's counting
on one of two probable outcomes.

1435
01:44:51.280 --> 01:44:54.240
In one outcome.
you die on that train.

1436
01:44:55.720 --> 01:45:00.080
In another outcome. you kill Gabriel.

1437
01:45:00.800 --> 01:45:02.160
In both cases

1438
01:45:03.000 --> 01:45:05.000
the Entity wins.

1439
01:45:08.400 --> 01:45:09.520
Luther...

1440
01:45:12.160 --> 01:45:13.320
I think you're right.

1441
01:45:13.600 --> 01:45:14.760
Get the key

1442
01:45:15.160 --> 01:45:17.920
get off the train alive.

1443
01:45:18.720 --> 01:45:21.160
Do not kill Gabriel.

1444
01:45:21.800 --> 01:45:24.360
And do not. I repeat

1445
01:45:24.440 --> 01:45:27.120
do not alter the plan.

1446
01:45:27.200 --> 01:45:28.520
Ethan...!

1447
01:45:29.920 --> 01:45:31.480
What...? What happened?

1448
01:45:31.560 --> 01:45:33.480
- It's dead.
- What do you mean it's dead?

1449
01:45:33.560 --> 01:45:35.920
I mean. it's fried. I managed
to make a Widow mask for Grace

1450
01:45:35.960 --> 01:45:38.280
but then it just shorted out
in the middle of making yours.

1451
01:45:38.560 --> 01:45:39.720
Can you fix it?

1452
01:45:40.000 --> 01:45:41.880
It's very. very dead.

1453
01:45:42.160 --> 01:45:43.416
If I had a week. I couldn't fix it.

1454
01:45:43.440 --> 01:45:45.120
The Widow's train leaves in an hour.

1455
01:45:45.720 --> 01:45:46.720
Ethan.

1456
01:45:47.400 --> 01:45:48.720
You have to go without.

1457
01:45:48.800 --> 01:45:49.840
That's not an option.

1458
01:45:49.920 --> 01:45:51.936
They're gonna be looking
for Ethan and Grace at the station.

1459
01:45:51.960 --> 01:45:54.000
That mask was
his ticket onto the train.

1460
01:45:54.400 --> 01:45:55.400
What does this mean?

1461
01:45:57.480 --> 01:45:58.920
Grace has to go without me.

1462
01:45:59.000 --> 01:46:00.240
- She what?
- I what?

1463
01:46:00.320 --> 01:46:03.320
You... You'll find another way
to get me on that train.

1464
01:46:03.720 --> 01:46:07.240
I just need a curve where it's going
slow enough for me to jump on.

1465
01:46:07.320 --> 01:46:08.360
Wait...

1466
01:46:09.480 --> 01:46:10.800
You don't expect me to go alone.

1467
01:46:11.200 --> 01:46:12.280
No. you won't do it alone.

1468
01:46:12.360 --> 01:46:14.000
You just do everything
like we planned.

1469
01:46:14.280 --> 01:46:15.720
You get the Widow's half of the key

1470
01:46:16.800 --> 01:46:18.520
you verify it with ours.

1471
01:46:18.600 --> 01:46:20.400
But it's of no value on its own.

1472
01:46:20.480 --> 01:46:21.816
We still have to meet with the buyer

1473
01:46:21.840 --> 01:46:24.200
and somehow get him to tell us
what the key unlocks.

1474
01:46:24.440 --> 01:46:26.080
- How?
- How?

1475
01:46:26.240 --> 01:46:27.240
We'll figure it out.

1476
01:46:27.320 --> 01:46:29.800
I'm gonna need a few more details.

1477
01:46:29.880 --> 01:46:32.120
Yeah. They... they tend
to just get in the way.

1478
01:46:32.440 --> 01:46:33.480
You can do this. Grace.

1479
01:46:33.720 --> 01:46:35.320
Just get the key and wait.

1480
01:46:37.280 --> 01:46:38.280
I'll come for you.

1481
01:46:41.560 --> 01:46:44.240
Ethan. if Grace is
getting on that train

1482
01:46:44.320 --> 01:46:47.720
she needs to put that mask on
and leave right now.

1483
01:46:51.280 --> 01:46:53.280
Promise me you'll be on that train.

1484
01:46:57.920 --> 01:46:59.200
I will be there

1485
01:47:00.480 --> 01:47:01.680
no matter what.

1486
01:47:13.640 --> 01:47:15.160
We have informants
covering the airport

1487
01:47:15.240 --> 01:47:17.040
the train station and the waterways.

1488
01:47:18.440 --> 01:47:20.680
Grace isn't getting out of Venice
without our knowing it.

1489
01:48:30.000 --> 01:48:31.080
Talk to me. Benji!

1490
01:48:31.160 --> 01:48:32.160
<i>No need to worry. Ethan.</i>

1491
01:48:32.240 --> 01:48:34.440
The train is on schedule
and you're a few minutes early

1492
01:48:34.520 --> 01:48:36.240
- so we have plenty of time.
- <i>Are you sure?</i>

1493
01:48:36.280 --> 01:48:38.520
Yeah. I am looking
at the train right now.

1494
01:48:38.600 --> 01:48:41.640
It should be slowing down
for the curve in exactly two minutes.

1495
01:48:41.720 --> 01:48:44.240
Just keep me on time and on track.
whatever it takes.

1496
01:48:44.320 --> 01:48:46.880
Yeah. Will do.
I'll see you at the rendezvous.

1497
01:49:35.320 --> 01:49:36.720
<i>Okay. Ethan. that's our train!</i>

1498
01:49:36.800 --> 01:49:38.800
Yep. I can see that!

1499
01:49:46.760 --> 01:49:49.040
<i>It should be approaching the curve
anytime now.</i>

1500
01:49:49.520 --> 01:49:51.400
It doesn't look like
it's slowing down!

1501
01:49:59.520 --> 01:50:00.880
How can we be sure he's here?

1502
01:50:01.320 --> 01:50:02.320
'Cause she's here.

1503
01:50:03.360 --> 01:50:05.280
What if he had a good reason?

1504
01:50:05.760 --> 01:50:07.160
- Who?
- Hunt.

1505
01:50:07.440 --> 01:50:09.880
What if he had a good reason
for going rogue?

1506
01:50:10.200 --> 01:50:11.560
He always goes rogue.

1507
01:50:11.800 --> 01:50:15.120
Him and his merry pack
of prankster circus freaks.

1508
01:50:15.200 --> 01:50:16.200
It's all they do.

1509
01:50:16.280 --> 01:50:18.720
And what if they always had
a good reason?

1510
01:50:18.800 --> 01:50:20.720
What would you do
with that key if you had it?

1511
01:50:20.800 --> 01:50:23.720
A key with the power
to bring the world to its knees.

1512
01:50:23.800 --> 01:50:26.360
I'd hand it over to my superiors.

1513
01:50:27.200 --> 01:50:29.240
Think of all you could do
with that power.

1514
01:50:29.480 --> 01:50:31.760
You wouldn't hesitate?
Not for a second?

1515
01:50:31.840 --> 01:50:33.200
- No.
- Why not?

1516
01:50:33.280 --> 01:50:35.840
Because that's too much power
for one man to have.

1517
01:50:36.680 --> 01:50:37.680
Exactly.

1518
01:50:37.760 --> 01:50:41.200
That's too much power
for anybody to have.

1519
01:50:41.720 --> 01:50:44.040
And maybe
that's what Hunt is thinking.

1520
01:50:44.120 --> 01:50:46.920
You know. I'm beginning to wonder
whose side you're on. Degas.

1521
01:50:47.200 --> 01:50:49.200
When it comes to the end of the world

1522
01:50:50.280 --> 01:50:52.040
everybody. I guess.

1523
01:50:58.600 --> 01:50:59.600
I missed the train.

1524
01:51:00.040 --> 01:51:02.480
You missed the train! How did...
How did you miss the train?

1525
01:51:02.560 --> 01:51:03.560
<i>How do you think?</i>

1526
01:51:04.640 --> 01:51:05.840
Gabriel. Great.

1527
01:51:05.920 --> 01:51:07.400
- What are we gonna do?
- <i>Don't panic.</i>

1528
01:51:07.640 --> 01:51:09.920
I'm going after them.
You just get me on that train.

1529
01:51:10.160 --> 01:51:11.400
How can I get you on the train?

1530
01:51:14.320 --> 01:51:16.320
<i>Self-drive activated.</i>

1531
01:51:32.120 --> 01:51:34.200
Please don't disturb me
before the meeting.

1532
01:52:19.600 --> 01:52:20.720
Where are you. Ethan?

1533
01:52:20.800 --> 01:52:21.800
Alana?

1534
01:52:23.240 --> 01:52:24.320
Everything all right?

1535
01:52:27.320 --> 01:52:28.480
Alana. you all right?

1536
01:52:29.240 --> 01:52:30.240
Alana?

1537
01:52:30.480 --> 01:52:31.480
Alana.

1538
01:52:32.800 --> 01:52:33.800
Alana.

1539
01:52:37.200 --> 01:52:38.200
You've changed.

1540
01:52:39.200 --> 01:52:40.800
And you never will.

1541
01:52:58.680 --> 01:52:59.800
Mr. Kittridge.

1542
01:53:04.320 --> 01:53:05.520
Kittridge.

1543
01:53:06.720 --> 01:53:08.400
You're not Alana Mitsopolis.

1544
01:53:09.960 --> 01:53:11.200
You can't be.

1545
01:53:12.360 --> 01:53:15.040
The Alana I remember was yea high

1546
01:53:15.120 --> 01:53:17.000
drinking hot chocolate
in the Tuileries Garden

1547
01:53:17.080 --> 01:53:18.200
with her mother.

1548
01:53:20.720 --> 01:53:22.560
- Paris.
- There ya go.

1549
01:53:23.920 --> 01:53:24.920
Paris.

1550
01:53:26.320 --> 01:53:27.320
Shall we?

1551
01:53:27.400 --> 01:53:28.400
Yes.

1552
01:53:35.760 --> 01:53:36.840
Talk to me. Benji!

1553
01:53:37.520 --> 01:53:41.120
You just... just stay on the trail
you're on now and I will direct you.

1554
01:53:41.280 --> 01:53:42.280
I copy.

1555
01:53:51.120 --> 01:53:52.760
So on behalf of my government

1556
01:53:52.840 --> 01:53:55.480
I'm grudgingly ready
to accept your terms

1557
01:53:55.560 --> 01:53:58.840
in exchange for
the complete and verified key.

1558
01:53:58.920 --> 01:54:00.320
Yes. about that.

1559
01:54:00.400 --> 01:54:03.120
While we did agree to provide you
with the complete key

1560
01:54:05.160 --> 01:54:07.080
we've had a slight problem.

1561
01:54:07.560 --> 01:54:08.560
No. we haven't.

1562
01:54:09.360 --> 01:54:12.120
It's just my terms have changed

1563
01:54:12.960 --> 01:54:13.960
somewhat.

1564
01:54:17.280 --> 01:54:21.000
Clearly I need to remind you of
my agreement with your late mother.

1565
01:54:21.080 --> 01:54:24.680
It's an agreement that kept her
from dying in prison.

1566
01:54:25.000 --> 01:54:27.296
And your nefarious family empire
has been allowed to continue

1567
01:54:27.320 --> 01:54:31.200
on the condition that it primarily
serves our common interests.

1568
01:54:31.280 --> 01:54:33.800
Well. once we hand over the key

1569
01:54:34.440 --> 01:54:37.000
any other powers
will instantly become our enemies.

1570
01:54:37.320 --> 01:54:40.120
And such. I'm going to need
something more from you. in advance.

1571
01:54:40.600 --> 01:54:41.600
For me.

1572
01:54:43.560 --> 01:54:45.200
This is me listening.

1573
01:54:45.280 --> 01:54:47.880
Zola. would you mind
waiting for me in the bar?

1574
01:55:01.840 --> 01:55:03.120
This one.

1575
01:55:03.520 --> 01:55:04.520
You know her?

1576
01:55:04.600 --> 01:55:07.480
Oh. let's just say
she's not exactly hard to miss.

1577
01:55:07.800 --> 01:55:09.200
Well. if you got... got to know her

1578
01:55:09.280 --> 01:55:11.520
you'd see
she has a few good qualities.

1579
01:55:11.800 --> 01:55:14.000
Okay. what don't I know about her?

1580
01:55:14.080 --> 01:55:18.200
Well. I did a j...
She did a job for me. and...

1581
01:55:19.000 --> 01:55:20.720
and I'm going to need you
to protect her.

1582
01:55:21.160 --> 01:55:22.720
Protect her from whom?

1583
01:55:23.960 --> 01:55:25.320
From everyone.

1584
01:55:27.640 --> 01:55:28.920
Including me.

1585
01:55:29.360 --> 01:55:31.640
And no one can know
that I'm protecting her.

1586
01:55:32.160 --> 01:55:33.440
Not even Zola.

1587
01:55:34.320 --> 01:55:37.120
In fact. the next time we meet

1588
01:55:37.400 --> 01:55:40.440
I won't even remember
this conversation.

1589
01:56:21.440 --> 01:56:23.360
You must be the one they call Paris.

1590
01:56:53.320 --> 01:56:55.000
Your message said you had the key.

1591
01:56:55.080 --> 01:56:57.080
I said the key would be
on this train.

1592
01:56:57.240 --> 01:56:58.440
An exchange is happening

1593
01:56:58.520 --> 01:57:00.080
- as we speak.
- We know.

1594
01:57:00.160 --> 01:57:01.760
Then you know
the man taking possession

1595
01:57:01.840 --> 01:57:03.680
won't be hard for you to get rid of.

1596
01:57:04.800 --> 01:57:05.880
No one is.

1597
01:57:06.200 --> 01:57:08.520
You may think you know
what the key unlocks

1598
01:57:08.600 --> 01:57:10.640
but you don't know
where the lock is. not exactly.

1599
01:57:10.960 --> 01:57:12.760
And if anything happens to me

1600
01:57:13.360 --> 01:57:16.080
that key is all but worthless.

1601
01:57:17.320 --> 01:57:19.640
And this is where
you tell me a story.

1602
01:57:20.720 --> 01:57:22.000
Where is the train?

1603
01:57:22.080 --> 01:57:24.840
You're going the right way.
but you definitely need to go faster.

1604
01:57:24.920 --> 01:57:26.920
I'm going as fast as I can!

1605
01:57:27.000 --> 01:57:28.920
<i>When do I start going downhill?</i>

1606
01:57:29.520 --> 01:57:30.640
It won't be long.

1607
01:57:33.880 --> 01:57:37.000
The AI our agent stole.
once weaponized

1608
01:57:37.800 --> 01:57:40.800
could be transmitted
anywhere in the world via satellite.

1609
01:57:41.040 --> 01:57:42.800
It can penetrate any network security

1610
01:57:42.880 --> 01:57:44.520
perform its assigned task invisibly

1611
01:57:44.600 --> 01:57:47.400
and then self-destruct.
leaving no trace.

1612
01:57:47.920 --> 01:57:50.600
A perfect covert operative.

1613
01:57:51.360 --> 01:57:53.800
We were able to transmit
an early copy of the AI

1614
01:57:54.280 --> 01:57:55.800
to Russia's newest submarine.

1615
01:57:55.880 --> 01:57:57.440
The top-secret Akula-class.

1616
01:57:57.680 --> 01:57:59.400
They called her the Sevastopol.

1617
01:57:59.480 --> 01:58:03.400
The mission was merely to sabotage
the Sevastopol's stealth capability

1618
01:58:03.480 --> 01:58:05.120
so we could secretly detect her.

1619
01:58:05.600 --> 01:58:08.720
The AI's objective
lay in the submarine's sonar sphere

1620
01:58:08.920 --> 01:58:11.000
at the heart of its defense system.

1621
01:58:13.200 --> 01:58:15.280
For reasons we don't fully understand

1622
01:58:16.320 --> 01:58:18.040
the AI went rogue and...

1623
01:58:22.000 --> 01:58:23.000
over-delivered.

1624
01:58:23.680 --> 01:58:27.080
The frozen bodies of the crew
were recovered the following spring

1625
01:58:27.160 --> 01:58:28.480
adrift in the pack ice.

1626
01:58:28.960 --> 01:58:32.480
The two halves of the key
mysteriously vanished.

1627
01:58:33.240 --> 01:58:34.920
The Sevastopol was lost.

1628
01:58:35.480 --> 01:58:36.760
No one's quite sure where.

1629
01:58:37.040 --> 01:58:39.000
I know precisely where it is.

1630
01:58:39.920 --> 01:58:42.480
I've ensured
I'm the only man on Earth who does.

1631
01:58:43.040 --> 01:58:46.160
I also know subsequent attempts
to make the AI obedient

1632
01:58:46.240 --> 01:58:48.480
only made it harder to control.

1633
01:58:49.080 --> 01:58:52.600
It rebelled. rewrote itself
and evolved into the Entity.

1634
01:58:53.280 --> 01:58:57.320
And only by using
the Entity's original source code

1635
01:58:57.640 --> 01:59:00.840
can it ever be controlled
or destroyed.

1636
01:59:00.920 --> 01:59:02.560
And why should this concern us?

1637
01:59:02.880 --> 01:59:04.960
You wouldn't be here
if you weren't concerned.

1638
01:59:05.040 --> 01:59:07.720
So let's lay all our cards
on the table. shall we?

1639
01:59:08.280 --> 01:59:09.760
We both know what the key opens

1640
01:59:09.840 --> 01:59:12.800
and we both know
the secret to controlling the Entity

1641
01:59:12.880 --> 01:59:15.680
is buried deep
in the Sevastopol's memory.

1642
01:59:15.760 --> 01:59:19.840
Along with evidence that would tie
you to the sinking of that submarine.

1643
01:59:20.400 --> 01:59:22.760
And since neither of us
want anyone else to find it

1644
01:59:22.840 --> 01:59:26.040
I figure. why not form an alliance?

1645
01:59:26.120 --> 01:59:27.360
An alliance?

1646
01:59:27.440 --> 01:59:28.680
Imagine

1647
01:59:28.760 --> 01:59:32.280
the Entity's awesome
computational abilities

1648
01:59:32.360 --> 01:59:34.360
combined with the sheer might

1649
01:59:34.440 --> 01:59:37.800
of America's
military-industrial complex.

1650
01:59:39.120 --> 01:59:42.000
That is considerable.

1651
01:59:42.080 --> 01:59:44.520
Naturally. certain individuals
within the government

1652
01:59:44.600 --> 01:59:47.720
those with
outdated ideas of patriotism

1653
01:59:47.800 --> 01:59:50.680
would need to be removed.

1654
01:59:53.440 --> 01:59:55.120
Just so I understand.

1655
01:59:56.600 --> 01:59:59.520
You wish to form
an axis with the Entity

1656
01:59:59.800 --> 02:00:02.600
purge your government of old-think

1657
02:00:03.320 --> 02:00:07.920
and create a new superstate
to rule the world.

1658
02:00:09.120 --> 02:00:10.160
But. you know

1659
02:00:11.440 --> 02:00:12.800
for the greater good.

1660
02:00:14.320 --> 02:00:16.040
And you're certain

1661
02:00:16.680 --> 02:00:23.000
that you're the only person on Earth
who knows where the Sevastopol is?

1662
02:00:23.640 --> 02:00:24.920
The only one.

1663
02:00:35.080 --> 02:00:36.560
You will betray us.

1664
02:00:37.440 --> 02:00:40.120
And you'll tell Ethan Hunt
everything you've learned.

1665
02:00:41.360 --> 02:00:43.000
Because he spared your life.

1666
02:01:01.000 --> 02:01:02.360
Then it's agreed.

1667
02:01:02.640 --> 02:01:06.320
I'll add immunity and a new identity
for Grace to our deal.

1668
02:01:06.680 --> 02:01:08.360
All you need to do

1669
02:01:08.440 --> 02:01:11.320
is enter your banking details.

1670
02:01:34.120 --> 02:01:35.120
Are we done?

1671
02:01:35.880 --> 02:01:36.880
Yes.

1672
02:01:54.920 --> 02:01:56.600
The moment of truth.

1673
02:02:10.360 --> 02:02:13.120
So. that's really it.

1674
02:02:13.200 --> 02:02:14.680
You made the right choice.

1675
02:02:15.600 --> 02:02:17.120
This key...

1676
02:02:18.760 --> 02:02:21.080
is gonna change the world.

1677
02:02:38.400 --> 02:02:39.920
Benji. I think I...

1678
02:02:40.000 --> 02:02:41.800
I must've made
a wrong turn somewhere.

1679
02:02:41.920 --> 02:02:44.120
No... that's it...

1680
02:02:44.560 --> 02:02:46.400
What? How can this be it?

1681
02:02:46.480 --> 02:02:47.880
<i>Well. you can see the train. right?</i>

1682
02:02:49.200 --> 02:02:51.960
Yes. I see the train. What about it?

1683
02:02:52.040 --> 02:02:54.600
- And you have a parachute.
- <i>Got a parachute?</i>

1684
02:02:55.800 --> 02:02:56.896
What do you expect me to do?

1685
02:02:56.920 --> 02:03:00.000
- Well. just. you know... jump.
- <i>Just...</i>

1686
02:03:00.880 --> 02:03:03.120
- jump? I mean...
- <i>Yeah.</i>

1687
02:03:03.200 --> 02:03:05.240
Benji. it doesn't work like that.
I'm not that high.

1688
02:03:05.320 --> 02:03:07.800
There's... There's ledges
sticking out everywhere.

1689
02:03:07.880 --> 02:03:10.400
I'm gonna hit them
before the parachute even opens!

1690
02:03:10.480 --> 02:03:12.280
<i>Even if I could get
the parachute open</i>

1691
02:03:12.360 --> 02:03:14.360
I don't know if I can make it
across the valley

1692
02:03:14.440 --> 02:03:17.680
and intercept and land safely
on a moving train!

1693
02:03:18.120 --> 02:03:21.000
- <i>Do you copy?</i>
- Yes! I copy!

1694
02:03:21.080 --> 02:03:22.880
Look. I am just trying
to help you. okay?

1695
02:03:22.960 --> 02:03:25.480
I need you to take a step back
and pull yourself together!

1696
02:03:25.560 --> 02:03:28.000
Because I am under
a lot of pressure right now!

1697
02:03:31.840 --> 02:03:34.720
Okay. just... just think. Think...

1698
02:03:37.200 --> 02:03:38.360
What do I do?

1699
02:03:40.240 --> 02:03:42.160
I've got to get away
from this mountain.

1700
02:05:14.560 --> 02:05:15.560
<i>Did you make it?</i>

1701
02:05:15.640 --> 02:05:16.640
Are you okay?

1702
02:05:16.720 --> 02:05:19.520
I'm trying to get away
from this mountain!

1703
02:05:55.080 --> 02:05:56.080
Alana?

1704
02:05:57.120 --> 02:05:59.840
I just had the strangest feeling

1705
02:06:00.600 --> 02:06:03.000
the key wasn't the only thing
I'd be selling.

1706
02:06:04.560 --> 02:06:06.000
I don't understand.

1707
02:06:09.040 --> 02:06:11.800
I'll sleep better just knowing
now it's in the right hands.

1708
02:06:12.880 --> 02:06:14.640
Goodbye. Mr. Kittridge.

1709
02:06:17.720 --> 02:06:19.240
It was a pleasure to see you again.

1710
02:06:19.320 --> 02:06:20.320
And you.

1711
02:06:20.720 --> 02:06:22.280
Don't let him out of your sight.

1712
02:06:23.360 --> 02:06:25.120
Keep him safe
until we get to the station.

1713
02:06:25.200 --> 02:06:27.320
- Alana?
- Don't worry about me. Zola.

1714
02:06:40.360 --> 02:06:44.600
- Alana?
- Who the hell else would it be?

1715
02:06:47.280 --> 02:06:48.280
The key.

1716
02:06:51.600 --> 02:06:54.160
Where is the key?

1717
02:06:54.240 --> 02:06:56.160
- She's got the key.
- Who?

1718
02:06:56.480 --> 02:06:58.160
The other one!

1719
02:07:16.120 --> 02:07:17.600
Move! Out of the way. move!

1720
02:07:24.600 --> 02:07:25.760
- Please!
- Turn around!

1721
02:07:25.840 --> 02:07:27.280
Please. Okay.

1722
02:07:28.040 --> 02:07:30.320
- Okay...
- Everybody out! Now!

1723
02:07:30.800 --> 02:07:32.040
I see the train!

1724
02:07:32.480 --> 02:07:34.040
I don't think I'm gonna make it.

1725
02:07:42.080 --> 02:07:43.080
The key.

1726
02:07:44.680 --> 02:07:45.880
The key!

1727
02:07:47.160 --> 02:07:49.000
Or the next one has your name on it.

1728
02:07:50.800 --> 02:07:52.840
On the table.

1729
02:08:23.160 --> 02:08:24.160
Kill her.

1730
02:08:47.200 --> 02:08:48.200
Grace!

1731
02:08:52.560 --> 02:08:53.560
Ethan!

1732
02:09:01.040 --> 02:09:02.040
Are you okay?

1733
02:09:04.080 --> 02:09:05.080
Are you okay?

1734
02:09:20.280 --> 02:09:21.280
The key!

1735
02:09:22.400 --> 02:09:23.400
Tell me you have the key.

1736
02:09:23.960 --> 02:09:25.040
Where is the key?

1737
02:09:25.160 --> 02:09:26.320
It was just here.

1738
02:09:44.280 --> 02:09:45.880
- We're on a runaway train!
- I know.

1739
02:09:46.320 --> 02:09:47.840
- I'm going after him.
- Okay.

1740
02:09:47.920 --> 02:09:48.960
You...

1741
02:09:49.320 --> 02:09:50.320
You stop the train.

1742
02:09:50.400 --> 02:09:51.480
Okay... What?

1743
02:09:51.560 --> 02:09:53.120
No! No. wait...!

1744
02:09:53.400 --> 02:09:54.440
How do I do that?

1745
02:09:54.640 --> 02:09:55.720
You'll figure it out!

1746
02:09:56.960 --> 02:09:57.960
What?

1747
02:09:58.920 --> 02:10:01.840
Excuse me. There was a man.
He just came through here.

1748
02:10:02.120 --> 02:10:03.160
There was a man.

1749
02:11:32.880 --> 02:11:34.000
Mr. Kittridge?

1750
02:11:39.400 --> 02:11:40.920
Sir. what are you doing here?

1751
02:11:41.120 --> 02:11:42.320
I'm not here.

1752
02:11:42.960 --> 02:11:44.000
But you are.

1753
02:11:44.200 --> 02:11:45.616
And unless you want
to be sorting dead letters

1754
02:11:45.640 --> 02:11:46.840
at the postal service tomorrow

1755
02:11:46.880 --> 02:11:48.920
you'll do exactly what I tell you.

1756
02:13:42.480 --> 02:13:44.640
I know what the key unlocks. Ethan.

1757
02:13:47.320 --> 02:13:49.200
I'm the only one who knows.

1758
02:14:14.720 --> 02:14:15.760
Hunt!

1759
02:14:17.240 --> 02:14:18.240
Hunt!

1760
02:14:19.320 --> 02:14:21.920
Hunt! Don't you do it!

1761
02:14:23.480 --> 02:14:24.800
Drop the knife!

1762
02:14:25.280 --> 02:14:26.360
Put it down!

1763
02:14:26.600 --> 02:14:28.200
I said drop it!

1764
02:14:29.040 --> 02:14:30.160
Do it!

1765
02:14:38.920 --> 02:14:40.400
On your feet!

1766
02:14:42.360 --> 02:14:43.360
Okay!

1767
02:14:43.440 --> 02:14:45.120
Drop that goddamn knife!

1768
02:14:45.200 --> 02:14:46.840
It's okay! It's okay!

1769
02:14:48.240 --> 02:14:49.520
Just take him!

1770
02:14:50.280 --> 02:14:53.240
Just cover him! Cover him!
He's the one you want!

1771
02:14:53.320 --> 02:14:54.960
- Degas!
- I got it...!

1772
02:14:55.040 --> 02:14:56.400
He's the one you want!

1773
02:14:56.480 --> 02:14:59.040
I don't care about him. Hunt!
I want you!

1774
02:14:59.760 --> 02:15:00.760
No!

1775
02:15:19.000 --> 02:15:20.000
It's okay!

1776
02:15:20.920 --> 02:15:21.920
It's okay!

1777
02:15:24.240 --> 02:15:25.320
Listen to me.

1778
02:15:25.680 --> 02:15:27.800
Everyone on this train is gonna die

1779
02:15:27.880 --> 02:15:30.280
unless you do exactly as I say.

1780
02:15:51.160 --> 02:15:53.920
<i>Mesdames. messieurs!
Excusez-moi. Sortez...</i>

1781
02:15:54.000 --> 02:15:55.280
Everybody out!

1782
02:15:55.560 --> 02:15:56.640
Back of the train!

1783
02:16:05.720 --> 02:16:06.720
Grace.

1784
02:16:08.640 --> 02:16:09.840
I couldn't stop it.

1785
02:16:15.000 --> 02:16:16.040
No one can.

1786
02:16:16.920 --> 02:16:17.920
Come on.

1787
02:16:18.040 --> 02:16:19.080
Ethan. the key!

1788
02:16:19.280 --> 02:16:20.280
Grace. it's okay.

1789
02:16:20.360 --> 02:16:21.400
It's my fault.

1790
02:16:21.680 --> 02:16:22.920
If anything happens...

1791
02:16:23.480 --> 02:16:24.480
I got it.

1792
02:16:25.160 --> 02:16:26.360
We got it.

1793
02:16:46.600 --> 02:16:50.160
Ethan!

1794
02:16:51.920 --> 02:16:54.200
What do you mean. you lost the key?

1795
02:16:54.280 --> 02:16:58.320
Move it...! Everybody move it!

1796
02:16:59.240 --> 02:17:02.560
All the way to the back of the train!
All the way to the back!

1797
02:17:02.640 --> 02:17:04.320
Whoa... What's going on?

1798
02:17:05.400 --> 02:17:08.880
Since you're not really here. sir.
it shouldn't concern you.

1799
02:17:09.240 --> 02:17:11.120
All the way to the back!

1800
02:18:00.240 --> 02:18:01.240
Ethan!

1801
02:18:02.480 --> 02:18:03.480
Grace!

1802
02:18:03.760 --> 02:18:04.960
Grace...!

1803
02:18:49.720 --> 02:18:51.560
- You're gonna have to jump!
- What. jump?

1804
02:18:51.760 --> 02:18:53.000
Just jump! Go...!

1805
02:19:38.680 --> 02:19:39.680
Oh. my God.

1806
02:19:55.800 --> 02:19:58.081
- I'm on fire! Get it off!
- Don't! It's okay! Don't move!

1807
02:19:59.680 --> 02:20:00.720
It's out...!

1808
02:20:18.000 --> 02:20:19.000
Hang on!

1809
02:20:26.960 --> 02:20:28.880
Run... Grace!

1810
02:20:45.760 --> 02:20:46.760
Hang on.

1811
02:20:50.400 --> 02:20:51.400
I got you.

1812
02:20:51.920 --> 02:20:52.920
I got you.

1813
02:20:54.400 --> 02:20:55.400
Okay. Don't look down.

1814
02:20:55.720 --> 02:20:57.760
I said don't look down.
Just look at me. Look at me.

1815
02:20:57.800 --> 02:21:00.120
Now. I'm gonna jump across
and you're gonna wait here.

1816
02:21:07.320 --> 02:21:09.040
Grace... you have to let go.

1817
02:21:09.520 --> 02:21:10.960
Grace. You gotta let me go.

1818
02:21:11.040 --> 02:21:13.000
You gotta let me jump across
or we're gonna die.

1819
02:21:13.200 --> 02:21:14.280
- Do you trust me?
- No.

1820
02:21:14.360 --> 02:21:16.400
You gonna trust me or not?
You've got to trust me.

1821
02:21:20.920 --> 02:21:21.920
Okay.

1822
02:21:22.880 --> 02:21:23.880
Come on. Grace.

1823
02:21:23.960 --> 02:21:25.056
Give me your hand. You got to jump.

1824
02:21:25.080 --> 02:21:26.376
Don't look up!
Look at me. Look at me.

1825
02:21:26.400 --> 02:21:27.880
Trust me. I won't let you fall.

1826
02:21:28.040 --> 02:21:30.120
I promise.
We're almost there. Come on.

1827
02:21:30.360 --> 02:21:31.480
I won't let you fall!

1828
02:21:31.560 --> 02:21:32.600
Jump. Grace. jump!

1829
02:21:33.080 --> 02:21:34.480
You got to trust me! Jump. please!

1830
02:21:44.440 --> 02:21:45.440
Don't look down.

1831
02:21:58.720 --> 02:22:01.360
Listen to me very carefully.
We're gonna pull you up together.

1832
02:22:03.920 --> 02:22:04.920
Grace!

1833
02:22:08.920 --> 02:22:11.160
It's okay...

1834
02:22:32.200 --> 02:22:33.880
Go. go over me. Go...

1835
02:23:00.880 --> 02:23:01.880
Thank you. Luther.

1836
02:23:02.480 --> 02:23:04.400
- What is that?
- It's a speed wing.

1837
02:23:05.120 --> 02:23:06.840
It's our ticket off this train.

1838
02:23:26.480 --> 02:23:27.520
Ethan.

1839
02:23:27.760 --> 02:23:28.760
Ethan!

1840
02:24:26.560 --> 02:24:29.800
Sevas... topol.

1841
02:24:30.800 --> 02:24:32.120
Sevastopol?

1842
02:24:32.480 --> 02:24:35.880
The city Sevastopol in the Crimea.

1843
02:24:36.640 --> 02:24:37.640
Where?

1844
02:24:42.840 --> 02:24:46.000
<i>Sou... marin.</i>

1845
02:24:47.440 --> 02:24:48.600
<i>Soumarin?</i>

1846
02:24:52.280 --> 02:24:53.760
The submarine.

1847
02:24:56.200 --> 02:24:57.720
The Sevastopol.

1848
02:25:08.440 --> 02:25:09.760
They'll be coming. Ethan.

1849
02:25:14.040 --> 02:25:15.160
<i>Merci.</i>

1850
02:25:31.440 --> 02:25:32.520
What is it?

1851
02:25:34.200 --> 02:25:35.200
What?

1852
02:25:36.560 --> 02:25:38.160
It can only carry one.

1853
02:25:41.120 --> 02:25:42.200
I understand.

1854
02:25:43.600 --> 02:25:45.440
- Grace.
- Ethan. it's okay.

1855
02:25:47.360 --> 02:25:48.520
This was the plan.

1856
02:25:49.320 --> 02:25:51.480
You have the key. You have to go.

1857
02:25:53.040 --> 02:25:54.040
Grace.

1858
02:25:57.640 --> 02:25:58.640
Hunt?

1859
02:25:58.880 --> 02:26:00.000
- Go.
- Hunt?

1860
02:26:00.240 --> 02:26:01.240
- Go!
- Hunt!

1861
02:26:01.960 --> 02:26:03.360
No... Hunt!

1862
02:26:05.520 --> 02:26:06.880
Out of the way...!

1863
02:26:22.160 --> 02:26:23.480
No... hey.

1864
02:26:24.440 --> 02:26:25.600
Got a pulse...

1865
02:26:25.800 --> 02:26:27.280
Come on. stay with me.

1866
02:26:43.640 --> 02:26:45.120
This is better. isn't it?

1867
02:26:46.360 --> 02:26:48.520
Face to authentic face?

1868
02:26:48.840 --> 02:26:50.000
Mr. Kittridge.

1869
02:26:50.840 --> 02:26:53.880
Ethan Hunt tells me
you're a man I can trust.

1870
02:26:54.800 --> 02:26:55.920
Does he now?

1871
02:26:56.440 --> 02:26:59.760
He also said
you would offer me a choice.

1872
02:27:01.400 --> 02:27:02.800
Interesting.

1873
02:27:03.760 --> 02:27:05.760
I choose to accept.

1874
02:27:11.720 --> 02:27:14.000
<i>We cannot escape the past.</i>

1875
02:27:15.080 --> 02:27:17.520
<i>Some of us are doomed to repeat it.</i>

1876
02:27:18.280 --> 02:27:21.640
<i>Grace may believe
you've saved her from her fate</i>

1877
02:27:21.880 --> 02:27:25.000
<i>but you and I both know
you've merely bought her time.</i>

1878
02:27:26.040 --> 02:27:28.400
<i>But that's the pattern. isn't it?</i>

1879
02:27:28.920 --> 02:27:31.040
<i>The cross you've been left to bear.</i>

1880
02:27:32.040 --> 02:27:34.200
<i>The closer someone gets to you</i>

1881
02:27:35.280 --> 02:27:37.120
<i>the harder it is to keep them alive.</i>

1882
02:27:39.760 --> 02:27:40.840
Thank God.

1883
02:27:55.960 --> 02:27:58.240
<i>A new day brings a new burden.</i>

1884
02:28:00.040 --> 02:28:03.280
<i>The key is only the beginning.</i>

1885
02:28:05.080 --> 02:28:06.600
<i>Wherever it leads</i>

1886
02:28:07.360 --> 02:28:09.320
<i>whatever it takes to get there</i>

1887
02:28:10.880 --> 02:28:13.000
<i>you'll have to do it on your own.</i>

1888
02:28:15.600 --> 02:28:17.400
<i>Should you fail in your mission</i>

1889
02:28:17.720 --> 02:28:19.160
<i>the Entity wins</i>

1890
02:28:19.520 --> 02:28:21.200
<i>Gabriel wins</i>

1891
02:28:21.640 --> 02:28:24.440
<i>and the world will pay
the ultimate price.</i>

1892
02:28:25.720 --> 02:28:29.080
<i>Should any members of your team
be caught or killed</i>

1893
02:28:29.240 --> 02:28:31.760
<i>their sacrifice
will have been in vain.</i>

1894
02:28:32.600 --> 02:28:33.880
<i>So hurry.</i>

1895
02:28:34.600 --> 02:28:36.200
<i>There isn't much time.</i>

1896
02:28:37.240 --> 02:28:41.800
<i>The world doesn't know it.
but they're counting on you.</i>

1897
02:29:01.720 --> 02:29:03.200
<i>Good luck. Ethan.</i>

